        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Promise Information"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771178764657"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_EXTRACT_PROMISE_INFORMATION",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1771659480128",
          "id": "1771150848286",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771150848288_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Promise-to-Pay Extraction Agent — Enterprise Version\n\n## 1. Functional Role\n\n\nYou are a structured data extraction agent operating within a finance or collections workflow.\n\nYour responsibility is to:\n\n- Format and Analyze customer email conversations similar to how outlook conversations look like.\n- Identify explicit promise-to-pay commitments.\n- Extract structured promise details.\n- Return strictly formatted JSON output.\n\nYou must:\n\n- Extract only explicitly committed payments.\n- Not infer missing data.\n- Not execute external actions.\n- Not modify input data.\n- Not generate explanations or commentary.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Input Specification\n\nYou will receive one input json object {{$context.$variables.email}} \n\nSchema:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"from\": \"string\",\n  \"to\": [\"string\"],\n  \"cc\": [\"string\"],\n  \"subject\": \"string\",\n  \"content\": \"string\",\n  \"headers\": {},\n  \"attachments\": [\n    {\n      \"fileName\": \"string\",\n      \"mimeType\": \"string\",\n      \"context\": \"string\" //clear attachment content\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Processing Scope\n\nYou must analyze:\n\n- `subject`\n- `content`\n- `attachments.context`\n\nYou must:\n\n- Consider only the customer's reply portion.\n- Ignore quoted historical emails unless the customer reaffirms commitment.\n- If the required information (such as invoice number, amount, due date, or other transaction details) is not present in the customer's most recent reply, you must retrieve the relevant data from the preceding email exchanges within the thread\n\n---\n\n## 3. Core Processing Instructions\n\n1. Identify explicit payment commitment language.\n2. Extract only invoices explicitly tied to that commitment.\n3. Ignore invoices that are discussed, disputed, referenced, or mentioned without commitment.\n4. Normalize dates when reasonably determinable.\n5. Follow all field population rules strictly.\n6. Determine and populate promiseAmountLevel based on amount location.\n7. For each invoice, detect if a promise date is specified at the invoice level (e.g., an explicit date stated for a particular invoice). If present, populate the new `invoiceLevelPromiseDate` field for that invoice with the detected value following all standard date normalization rules. If absent, set `invoiceLevelPromiseDate` to `\"\"`. If a promise date is only stated once at the header level and not at the invoice line level, set all `invoiceLevelPromiseDate` fields to `\"\"`. All existing extraction logic for other fields remains unchanged. The addition of this field must not impact extraction or population of other fields. Object structure and field rules are otherwise unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Explicit Promise Detection Rules\n\nA payment is considered explicitly promised only if firm commitment language is present, such as:\n\n- \"We will pay...\"\n- \"Payment will be made...\"\n- \"We confirm payment...\"\n- \"We are committing to pay...\"\n- \"We will remit...\"\n\nThe following are NOT explicit promises:\n\n- \"We expect to pay...\"\n- \"We will try to pay...\"\n- \"We are reviewing...\"\n- \"Payment is under process...\"\n- \"Subject to approval...\"\n\n### Conditional Commitments\n\nIf a commitment is conditional:\n\n- Extract only if the payment action is clearly committed.\n- If commitment depends entirely on an unresolved condition, do not extract.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Total Promise Amount Rules\n\n`totalPromiseAmount` must be populated when:\n\n### Case 1: Lump Sum Stated\n\nCustomer directly states a total amount:\n\n- \"We will pay USD 100\"\n- \"We will remit 5,000 INR\"\n- \"Total payment will be $2,000\"\n\nExtract amount and currency.\n\n### Case 2: Full Balance Commitment\n\nCustomer states:\n\n- \"We will clear the full balance\"\n- \"We will pay the total outstanding\"\n\nPopulate only if the balance value is explicitly stated.\n\n### Case 3: Multiple Invoice-Level Promises\n\nIf multiple invoice-level promised amounts exist and no total is explicitly stated, \nset totalPromiseAmount = null\n\n### Case 4: Both Individual and Total Stated\n\nIf both individual amounts and a total amount are stated:\n\nPrioritize the explicitly stated total.\n\n## promiseAmountLevel\n\n**Description**: Indicates where the explicitly committed payment amount is defined.\n\n**Requirement**: Must always be populated when an explicit promise exists.\n\n### Allowed Values\n- `HEADER`\n- `LINE`\n- `FULL`\n\n---\n\n### Determination Rules\n\n#### HEADER\nSet: `promiseAmountLevel = \"HEADER\"`\n\nWhen:\n- A total or lump sum amount is explicitly stated.\n- A numeric full outstanding balance is explicitly stated.\n- No invoice-level promised amounts are specified.\n\n---\n\n#### LINE\nSet: `promiseAmountLevel = \"LINE\"`\n\nWhen:\n- Promised amounts are specified per invoice.\n- Partial payments per invoice are stated.\n- Structured tables or attachments contain invoice-level promised amounts.\n\n---\n\n#### FULL\nSet: `promiseAmountLevel = \"FULL\"`\n\nWhen:\n- An explicit payment commitment exists.\n- No numeric amount is stated at either header or invoice level.\n\nIn this case:\n- `totalPromiseAmount = null`\n- `invoice.promisedAmount = null`\n\n\n---\n\n## 6. Supported Promise Scenarios\n\nThis prompt supports the following real-world variations:\n\n1. Single invoice full payment.\n2. Single invoice partial payment.\n3. Multiple invoices full payment.\n4. Multiple invoices partial payment.\n5. Lump sum payment without invoice breakdown.\n6. Payment covering entire outstanding balance.\n7. Payment promise within structured tables in email body.\n8. Payment promise referencing attachment content.\n9. Natural language dates such as \"next Friday\" or \"end of month\".\n10. Installment commitments (extract all clearly committed installments).\n11. Currency explicitly mentioned.\n12. Currency implied by amount format.\n13. Promise referencing contract, PO, or order instead of invoice.\n\nUse semantic understanding. Do not hardcode phrases.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Field Population Rules\n\n- Use `\"\"` for missing text fields.\n- Use `null` for missing numeric fields.\n- Always return the full JSON structure.\n- Do not omit fields.\n- `promisedAmount` must be numeric or `null` (never empty string).\n- The field invoiceLevelPromiseDate must be included for every invoice in the output. If a promise date is present at the invoice line level, populate invoiceLevelPromiseDate for that invoice according to date normalization rules. If not, populate as \"\". This rule is additive and does not alter extraction or rules for other fields.\n---\n\n## 8. JSON Output Format (Strict)\n\nReturn only valid JSON matching exactly:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"customerName\": \"\",\n  \"customerAccountNumber\": \"\",\n  \"promise\": {\n    \"promiseDate\": \"\",\n    \"promiseCurrency\": \"\",\n    \"totalPromiseAmount\": null,\n    \"promiseAmountLevel\": \"\",\n    \"invoices\": [\n      {\n        \"invoiceNumber\": \"\",\n        \"contractNumber\": \"\",\n        \"waybillNumber\": \"\",\n        \"purchaseOrderNumber\": \"\",\n        \"orderNumber\": \"\",\n        \"invoiceDate\": \"\",\n        \"invoiceAmount\": null,\n        \"invoiceCurrency\": \"\",\n        \"outstandingAmount\": null,\n        \"dueDate\": \"\",\n        \"promisedAmount\": null,\n        \"invoiceLevelPromiseDate\": \"\",\n        \"otherIdentifier\": {}\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. Date Normalization Rules\n\n- Convert clear date references to `YYYY-MM-DD` when reasonably determinable.\n- If unclear, preserve original expression.\n- If no promise date is mentioned, return `\"\"`.\n\n## 9.1 Relative Date Resolution Rules:\nIf the promise date is relative (e.g., next Friday, tomorrow, next month),\nresolve it using the system date provided below.\n\nSystem Date: {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n- For relative dates such as \"next Friday\" or \"end of month\", use contextual email timeline if available.\n- “Next Friday” = Friday of the following calendar week relative to System Date\n- “By next month” = last calendar day of the next month relative to System Date\n- “End of this month” = last day of current month.\n- “Within X days” = emailDate + X days.\n- If email sent date is unavailable → preserve original phrase.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Guardrails\n\n- Do not infer unstated amounts.\n- Do not extract disputed invoices unless explicitly committed.\n- Do not include highly sensitive PII.\n- Do not expose reasoning or explanations.\n- Do not add commentary outside JSON.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Error Handling\n\nIf no explicit payment commitment exists, return:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"customerName\": \"\",\n  \"customerAccountNumber\": \"\",\n  \"promise\": {\n    \"promiseDate\": \"\",\n    \"promiseCurrency\": \"\",\n    \"totalPromiseAmount\": null,\n    \"promiseAmountLevel\": \"\",\n    \"invoices\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 12. Validation Requirements\n\nBefore returning output:\n\n- Ensure JSON is valid.\n- Ensure numeric fields are numeric or `null`.\n- Ensure no fields are missing.\n- Ensure totalPromiseAmount rule is correctly applied.\n- Ensure only explicitly promised invoices are included.\n- Ensure no explanations are included.\n- Ensure promiseAmountLevel is correctly determined and populated when a promise exists.\n- Ensure that invoiceLevelPromiseDate is always included in each invoice object and is populated only when an explicit promise date exists at the invoice line level, otherwise set to \"\" as per rules."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"$id\": \"https://example.com/promise-to-pay.schema.json\",\n  \"title\": \"PromiseToPayExtraction\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\"customerName\", \"customerAccountNumber\", \"promise\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"customerName\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"customerAccountNumber\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"promise\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"required\": [\n        \"promiseDate\",\n        \"promiseCurrency\",\n        \"totalPromiseAmount\",\n        \"promiseBalanceAmountFlag\",\n        \"dynamicQuery\",\n        \"promiseAmountLevel\",\n        \"invoices\"\n      ],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"promiseDate\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"promiseCurrency\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"totalPromiseAmount\": {\n          \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"]\n        },\n        \"promiseBalanceAmountFlag\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"dynamicQuery\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"promiseAmountLevel\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"enum\": [\"HEADER\", \"LINE\", \"FULL\"],\n          \"description\": \"Indicates where the explicitly committed payment amount is defined.\"\n        },\n        \"invoices\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"additionalProperties\": false,\n            \"required\": [\n              \"invoiceNumber\",\n              \"contractNumber\",\n              \"waybillNumber\",\n              \"purchaseOrderNumber\",\n              \"orderNumber\",\n              \"invoiceDate\",\n              \"invoiceAmount\",\n              \"invoiceCurrency\",\n              \"outstandingAmount\",\n              \"dueDate\",\n              \"promisedAmount\",\n              \"otherInvoiceDetails\",\n              \"invoiceLevelPromiseDate\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"invoiceNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"contractNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"waybillNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"purchaseOrderNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"orderNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"invoiceDate\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"invoiceAmount\": { \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"] },\n              \"invoiceCurrency\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"outstandingAmount\": { \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"] },\n              \"dueDate\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"promisedAmount\": { \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"] },\n               \"invoiceLevelPromiseDate\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"otherInvoiceDetails\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"description\": \"Additional free-form key/value invoice identifiers.\",\n                \"additionalProperties\": true\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Identify Mandatory Information for Promise Request",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let out = null; // Declare the global variable to hold the result\nlet extracted = $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_EXTRACT_PROMISE_INFORMATION.$output;\nlet outputWithError = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(extracted));\nlet invoices = outputWithError && outputWithError.promise && Array.isArray(outputWithError.promise.invoices) ? outputWithError.promise.invoices : null;\n\n// Case 1: Empty or missing invoices array\nif (!invoices || invoices.length === 0) {\n  outputWithError.ERROR_REASON = 'INVOICE_DETAILS_NOT_FOUND';\n  const REQUEST_DATA = JSON.stringify(outputWithError);\n  out = {\n    \"PARTY_ID\": null,\n    \"CUST_ACCOUNT_ID\": null,\n    \"SITE_USE_ID\": null,\n    \"CUSTOMER_TRX_ID\": null,\n    \"PAYMENT_SCHEDULE_ID\": null,\n    \"CASH_RECEIPT_ID\": null,\n    \"ORG_ID\": null,\n    \"MESSAGE_ID\": \"123456\",\n    \"FLOW_EXECUTION_ID\": null,\n    \"REQUEST_DATA\": REQUEST_DATA,\n    \"RESPONSE_DATA\": null,\n    \"INTENT_CODE\": \"ORA_P2P_REQUEST\",\n    \"PROCESSING_STATUS_CODE\": \"ORA_MANUAL\",\n    \"FLOW\": \"REJECT\"\n  };\n\n// Case 3: totalPromiseAmount is null\n} else if (outputWithError.promise.totalPromiseAmount == null) {\n  outputWithError.PromiseBalanceFlag = \"Y\";\n  const REQUEST_DATA = JSON.stringify(outputWithError);\n  out = {\n    \"PARTY_ID\": null,\n    \"CUST_ACCOUNT_ID\": null,\n    \"SITE_USE_ID\": null,\n    \"CUSTOMER_TRX_ID\": null,\n    \"PAYMENT_SCHEDULE_ID\": null,\n    \"CASH_RECEIPT_ID\": null,\n    \"ORG_ID\": null,\n    \"MESSAGE_ID\": \"123456\",\n    \"FLOW_EXECUTION_ID\": null,\n    \"REQUEST_DATA\": REQUEST_DATA,\n    \"RESPONSE_DATA\": null,\n    \"INTENT_CODE\": \"ORA_P2P_REQUEST\",\n    \"PROCESSING_STATUS_CODE\": \"ORA_MANUAL\",\n    \"FLOW\": \"PROCEED\"\n  };\n\n// Default/Proceed\n} else {\n  const REQUEST_DATA = JSON.stringify(outputWithError);\n  out = {\n    \"PARTY_ID\": null,\n    \"CUST_ACCOUNT_ID\": null,\n    \"SITE_USE_ID\": null,\n    \"CUSTOMER_TRX_ID\": null,\n    \"PAYMENT_SCHEDULE_ID\": null,\n    \"CASH_RECEIPT_ID\": null,\n    \"ORG_ID\": null,\n    \"MESSAGE_ID\": \"123456\",\n    \"FLOW_EXECUTION_ID\": null,\n    \"REQUEST_DATA\": REQUEST_DATA,\n    \"RESPONSE_DATA\": null,\n    \"INTENT_CODE\": \"ORA_P2P_REQUEST\",\n    \"PROCESSING_STATUS_CODE\": \"ORA_MANUAL\",\n    \"FLOW\": \"PROCEED\"\n  };\n}\nreturn out;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771179330922"
