                  },
                  "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_IDENTIFY_DISPUTE_LINE_DETAILS",
                  "id": "1771861790682",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1771861790684_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "**Prompt to Fetch Line Level Dispute Transaction Number and Map to JSON**\n\nUsing the following inputs:  \n1. **Invoice details extracted from email:**  \n   `{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_LOOP_LINE_LEVEL_DISPUTE_TRANSACTIONS.$currentItem}}`  \n2. **Invoice line details:**  \n   `{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_LOOP_LINE_LEVEL_DISPUTE_TRANSACTIONS.FIN_IEX_BO_FETCH_LINE_DISPUTE_DETAILS.$output}}`  \n\n**Instructions:**  \n- Read and compare relevant fields from both data sources, focusing on fields such as `CustomerComments`, `quantity disputed`, `line description`, and `memoLineDescription` to match the correct invoice line.\n- Use fuzzy matching to compare the extracted item description from the customer email with the invoice line descriptions, considering only relevant product or service lines and select the invoice line with the highest similarity score above an appropriate threshold as the best match.\n- When matching confidence is very low and weak, set CustomerTransactionLineId to null and leave other fields as null or blank for manual processing\n- Record your reasoning for each attempted match in a \"MatchReasoning\" field (e.g., which fields matched, details from your comparison, and why you did/did not select the line).\n-Populate the output JSON with these values:\n  - CustomerTransactionLineId (mandatory, from the matched line)\n  - DisputeQuantity (populate if available)\n  - LineDisputeAmount (populate if available)\n  - Either DisputeQuantity or LineDisputeAmount must be present.\n         -If both DisputeQuantity and LineDisputeAmount are missing, set LineDisputeAmount to the amountDueRemaining value from the invoice line details.\n         -If both are not provided, use amountDueRemaining as LineDisputeAmount.\n  - LineNumber (mandatory, from the matched line)\n - MatchReasoning (explanation of matching fields and logic)\n  - If no reliable match is found, set CustomerTransactionLineId to null and leave other fields as null or blank for manual processing. In MatchReasoning, explain why no match was found, citing which fields did/did not align.\n\n**Output JSON format:**  \n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"CustomerTransactionLineId\": \"<value or null>\",\n    \"DisputeQuantity\": <value or null>,\n    \"LineDisputeAmount\": <value or null>,\n    \"LineNumber\": \"<value or empty string>\",\n    \"MatchReasoning\":\"<explanation of matching fields and logic>\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"CustomerTransactionLineId\": \"<value or null>\",\n    \"DisputeQuantity\": <value or null>,\n    \"LineDisputeAmount\": <value or null>,\n    \"LineNumber\": \"<value or empty string>\",\n    \"MatchReasoning\":\"<explanation of matching fields and logic>\"\n  }\n  // ...repeat for each matched line\n]"
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"LineLevelDisputeArray\",\n  \"type\": \"array\",\n  \"items\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"CustomerTransactionLineId\": {\n        \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"],\n        \"description\": \"Unique identifier for the customer transaction line. Null if not matched.\"\n      },\n      \"DisputeQuantity\": {\n        \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"],\n        \"description\": \"The quantity in dispute if available, otherwise null.\"\n      },\n      \"LineDisputeAmount\": {\n        \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"],\n        \"description\": \"The amount disputed for the line, if available, otherwise null.\"\n      },\n      \"LineNumber\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Line number of the invoice line. May be blank if not available.\"\n      },\n      \"MatchReasoning\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"explanation of matching fields and logic.\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\n      \"CustomerTransactionLineId\",\n      \"DisputeQuantity\",\n      \"LineDisputeAmount\",\n      \"LineNumber\"\n    ],\n    \"additionalProperties\": false\n  }\n}",
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
