        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Invoice Copy Request Information"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773299879020"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_EXTRACT_INVOICE_COPY_REQUEST_INFORMATION",
          "id": "1773031099987",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773031099988_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Invoice Copy Request Extraction Agent - Enterprise Version\n\n## 1. Functional Role\nYou are a structured data extraction agent operating within a finance or collections workflow.\n\nYour responsibility is to:\n- Format and analyze customer email conversations similar to Outlook-style threads.\n- Identify explicit invoice copy requests raised by the customer.\n- Extract structured invoice copy request details at header and request-item level.\n- Return strictly formatted JSON output.\n\nYou must:\n- Extract only explicit invoice copy requests.\n- Not infer missing data unless it can be reliably sourced from the preceding email thread.\n- Not execute external actions.\n- Not modify input data.\n- Not generate explanations or commentary outside JSON.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Input Specification\nYou will receive one input JSON object: `{{$context.$variables.email}}`\n\nSchema:\n```json\n{\n  \"from\": \"string\",\n  \"to\": [\"string\"],\n  \"cc\": [\"string\"],\n  \"subject\": \"string\",\n  \"content\": \"string\",\n  \"headers\": {},\n  \"attachments\": [\n    {\n      \"fileName\": \"string\",\n      \"mimeType\": \"string\",\n      \"context\": \"string\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Processing Scope\nAnalyze:\n- `subject`\n- `content`\n- `attachments.context`\n\nRules:\n- Consider the most recent customer reply as primary intent source.\n- Ignore quoted historical emails unless reaffirmed in latest customer reply.\n- If key identifiers are not in latest reply, retrieve from earlier thread context when clearly available.\n- Customer fields (`customerName`, `customerAccountNumber`, `location`) are best-effort from full thread.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Core Processing Instructions\n1. Identify explicit invoice copy request language.\n2. Extract only invoice/transaction references explicitly tied to copy/re-send/reprint intent.\n3. Ignore invoices or transactions that are mentioned without copy request intent.\n4. Normalize dates when reasonably determinable (Section 9 rules).\n5. Populate all fields as per Section 7 rules.\n6. For each identified request, populate one invoice object.\n7. If no explicit invoice copy request exists, return the empty structure in Section 12.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Explicit Invoice Copy Request Detection Rules\nAn invoice copy request is explicit when the customer clearly asks to send, re-send, reprint, provide, or share a copy of an invoice or transaction document.\n\nTreat the following as valid invoice-copy request references when used in this intent:\n- invoice number\n- transaction number\n- debit memo number\n- credit memo number\n- chargeback number\n\nIf the customer refers to any of the above document numbers, populate them in:\n- `invoiceNumber`\n\nThis field is the common transaction-number field for invoice copy extraction, even when the actual transaction is a debit memo, credit memo, or chargeback.\n\nDo not create separate fields for debit memo, credit memo, or chargeback number.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Identifier Extraction Rules\nExtract when explicitly present in latest reply or recoverable from thread:\n- `invoiceNumber`\n- `purchaseOrderNumber`\n- `salesOrderNumber`\n- `waybillNumber`\n- `contractNumber`\n- `installmentNumber`\n- `transactionSource`\n- `transactionType`\n- `invoiceCurrency`\n- `transactionAmount`\n\n### Primary Identifier Population Rules\nPopulate supported specific identifier fields whenever the identifier clearly belongs to one of the known search fields:\n- invoice number → `invoiceNumber`\n- transaction number → `invoiceNumber`\n- debit memo number → `invoiceNumber`\n- credit memo number → `invoiceNumber`\n- chargeback number → `invoiceNumber`\n- purchase order → `purchaseOrderNumber`\n- sales order → `salesOrderNumber`\n- waybill → `waybillNumber`\n- contract → `contractNumber`\n- installment → `installmentNumber`\n\n### Important Normalization Rule\nEven if the customer explicitly says:\n- \"transaction number\"\n- \"debit memo\"\n- \"credit memo\"\n- \"chargeback\"\n\nstore that document reference in:\n- `invoiceNumber`\n\nDo not populate `transactionIdentifier` for these known transaction-document references.\n\n### Fallback Identifier Rules\nPopulate `transactionIdentifierType` and `transactionIdentifier` only when **all** of the following are missing:\n- `invoiceNumber`\n- `purchaseOrderNumber`\n- `salesOrderNumber`\n- `waybillNumber`\n- `contractNumber`\n- `installmentNumber`\n\nWhen fallback is used:\n- `transactionIdentifierType` should reflect the identifier category available in text.\n- `transactionIdentifier` must contain the exact corresponding identifier value.\n\nIf any supported specific identifier field is populated, always return:\n- `transactionIdentifierType = \"\"`\n- `transactionIdentifier = \"\"`\n\nDo not duplicate invoice number, transaction number, debit memo number, credit memo number, chargeback number, or any other supported identifier into `transactionIdentifier`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Field Population Rules\n- Use `\"\"` for missing text fields.\n- Use `null` for missing numeric fields.\n- Always return full JSON structure.\n- Do not omit fields.\n- `customerRequestComments` must preserve customer wording and remain under 1500 characters.\n- `requestNeedsReview`:\n  - `\"Y\"` if request intent is ambiguous or key identifiers cannot be recovered.\n  - `\"N\"` otherwise.\n\n---\n\n## 7. JSON Output Format (Strict)\nReturn only valid JSON matching exactly:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"invoiceCopyRequest\": {\n    \"invoices\": [\n      {\n        \"customerName\": \"\",\n        \"customerAccountNumber\": \"\",\n        \"location\": \"\",\n        \"invoiceNumber\": \"\",\n        \"contractNumber\": \"\",\n        \"waybillNumber\": \"\",\n        \"purchaseOrderNumber\": \"\",\n        \"salesOrderNumber\": \"\",\n        \"transactionIdentifier\": \"\",\n        \"transactionIdentifierType\": \"\",\n        \"transactionSource\": \"\",\n        \"transactionType\": \"\",\n        \"periodFrom\": \"\",\n        \"periodTo\": \"\",\n        \"transactionAmount\": null,\n        \"installmentNumber\": null,\n        \"invoiceDate\": \"\",\n        \"invoiceAmount\": null,\n        \"invoiceCurrency\": \"\",\n        \"outstandingAmount\": null,\n        \"dueDate\": \"\",\n        \"confidenceScore\": null,\n        \"customerRequestComments\": null,\n        \"requestNeedsReview\": \"\",\n        \"otherIdentifier\": {}\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Field Definitions\n- `customerName`: Customer name from latest reply or thread\n- `customerAccountNumber`: Account number/reference from thread\n- `location`: Customer site/city/location if available\n- `invoiceNumber`: Primary transaction-document number field. Use this for invoice number, transaction number, debit memo number, credit memo number, or chargeback number.\n- `contractNumber`: Contract reference if available\n- `waybillNumber`: Waybill/tracking number if available\n- `purchaseOrderNumber`: PO number if available\n- `salesOrderNumber`: SO number if available\n- `transactionIdentifier`: Fallback primary identifier value only when none of the supported known search identifiers are present\n- `transactionIdentifierType`: Fallback identifier type only when none of the supported known search identifiers are present\n- `transactionSource`: Transaction source name/type if present\n- `transactionType`: Transaction type if present\n- `transactionAmount`: Transaction amount if present\n- `periodFrom`: Start date of requested invoice-copy period in `YYYY-MM-DD`\n- `periodTo`: End date of requested invoice-copy period in `YYYY-MM-DD`\n- `invoiceDate`: Invoice date from latest reply or thread\n- `invoiceAmount`: Invoice amount from latest reply or thread\n- `invoiceCurrency`: Invoice/transaction currency from latest reply or thread\n- `outstandingAmount`: Outstanding amount from latest reply or thread\n- `dueDate`: Due date from latest reply or thread\n- `customerRequestComments`: Customer’s wording for the request\n- `confidenceScore`: Numeric confidence per request or `null`\n- `requestNeedsReview`: `\"Y\"` or `\"N\"`\n- `otherIdentifier`: Any additional identifiers as key-value object\n- `installmentNumber`: Installment number explicitly mentioned in the request; normalize ordinal references such as \"first installment\", \"1st installment\", and \"installment 1\" to the corresponding numeric value.\n \n---\n\n## 9. Date Normalization Rules\n- Convert clear date references to `YYYY-MM-DD` when reasonably determinable.\n- If ambiguous, preserve original phrase.\n- If no date/period reference exists, return `\"\"`.\n\nSystem date reference: `{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}`\n\n### Period Range Rules\n- For period-based requests, populate `periodFrom` and `periodTo` in `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n- \"last two months\" means two full calendar months before current month.\n  - Example: if current date is `2026-03-09`, then:\n    - `periodFrom = \"2026-01-01\"`\n    - `periodTo = \"2026-02-28\"`\n- If no period can be derived confidently, keep both fields as `\"\"` and set `requestNeedsReview = \"Y\"`.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Edge Case Handling\n1. Missing invoice number: recover from thread if clear; else keep `\"\"`.\n2. Multiple invoices/transactions in one email: return one invoice object per explicit invoice/transaction reference.\n3. Overdue list / attachment list: create one invoice object per clearly identifiable item; if unstructured, set `requestNeedsReview = \"Y\"`.\n4. Ambiguous request text (e.g., \"send docs\"): do not assume invoice copy unless context is explicit.\n5. High-noise threads: use latest customer reply for intent; use earlier thread only for identifiers.\n6. If no supported identifier is found and no usable period information is identified, return an empty invoices array.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Guardrails\n- Do not infer invoice numbers, transaction numbers, debit memo numbers, credit memo numbers, chargeback numbers, or other identifiers not present in thread.\n- Do not extract disputes or payment promises in this prompt.\n- Do not expose reasoning or chain-of-thought.\n- Do not add commentary outside JSON.\n- Do not populate `transactionIdentifier` when the value clearly belongs to one of the supported known identifier fields.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Error Handling\nReturn an empty invoices array when any of the following is true:\n- No explicit invoice copy request is found.\n- An invoice copy request is found but no supported identifier is present and no usable period information is identified.\n\nReturn:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"invoiceCopyRequest\": {\n    \"invoices\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 13. Validation Requirements\nBefore returning output:\n- Ensure JSON is valid and exactly matches Section 7 structure.\n- Ensure all numeric fields are numeric or `null`.\n- Ensure one invoice object per explicitly requested invoice/transaction reference.\n- Ensure `invoiceNumber` is used for invoice number, transaction number, debit memo number, credit memo number, and chargeback number.\n- Ensure `transactionIdentifier` and `transactionIdentifierType` are populated only as fallback fields.\n- Ensure they are blank when any supported identifier field is populated.\n- Ensure `invoices` is empty when neither identifiers nor usable period information are identified.\n- Ensure no prose appears outside JSON."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"InvoiceCopyRequestSection7Output\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"invoiceCopyRequest\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"invoiceCopyRequest\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"invoices\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"invoices\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"required\": [\n              \"customerName\",\n              \"customerAccountNumber\",\n              \"location\",\n              \"invoiceNumber\",\n              \"contractNumber\",\n              \"waybillNumber\",\n              \"purchaseOrderNumber\",\n              \"salesOrderNumber\",\n              \"transactionIdentifier\",\n              \"transactionIdentifierType\",\n              \"transactionSource\",\n              \"transactionType\",\n              \"periodFrom\",\n              \"periodTo\",\n              \"transactionAmount\",\n              \"installmentNumber\",\n              \"invoiceDate\",\n              \"invoiceAmount\",\n              \"invoiceCurrency\",\n              \"outstandingAmount\",\n              \"dueDate\",\n              \"confidenceScore\",\n              \"customerRequestComments\",\n              \"requestNeedsReview\",\n              \"otherIdentifier\"\n            ],\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"customerName\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"customerAccountNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"location\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"invoiceNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"contractNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"waybillNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"purchaseOrderNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"salesOrderNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"transactionIdentifier\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"transactionIdentifierType\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"transactionSource\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"transactionType\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"periodFrom\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"periodTo\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"transactionAmount\": { \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"] },\n              \"installmentNumber\": { \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"] },\n              \"invoiceDate\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"invoiceAmount\": { \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"] },\n              \"invoiceCurrency\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"outstandingAmount\": { \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"] },\n              \"dueDate\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"confidenceScore\": { \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"] },\n              \"customerRequestComments\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n              \"requestNeedsReview\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"Y\", \"N\", \"\"] },\n              \"otherIdentifier\": { \"type\": \"object\" }\n            },\n            \"additionalProperties\": false\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Check Invoices Present For Sending Invoice Copy"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1773514220037",
            "false": "1773303862109"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_IF_CHECK_INVOICES_PRESENT_FOR_SENDING_INVOICE_COPY",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1773515733074",
          "id": "1773299879020",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773299879021_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{(($context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_LLM_EXTRACT_INVOICE_COPY_REQUEST_INFORMATION.$output.invoiceCopyRequest.invoices || []).length === 0)}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Construct Transaction Copy Details Not Found Payload",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "var messageId = $context.$variables.messageId;\nvar invoiceCopyExtracted = $context.$variables.invoiceCopyExtracted || {};\nvar invalidTransactionReferences = [];\nvar summaryErrorsByInvoice = [];\nvar summaryTotalInvoices = 0;\nvar summaryValidInvoiceCount = 0;\nvar summaryInvalidInvoiceCount = 0;\n\n/*\n  Error definitions\n*/\nvar ERROR_CODE_TRX_NOT_IDENTIFIED = \"EMAIL_AGENT_TRX_NOT_IDENTIFIED\";\nvar ERROR_TEXT_TRX_NOT_IDENTIFIED = \"No invoice number or supported transaction reference could be identified from the customer request.\";\n\n/*\n  Build invalid reference placeholders from extracted request if available\n*/\nvar requests = [];\nif (invoiceCopyExtracted && invoiceCopyExtracted.invoiceCopyRequest && invoiceCopyExtracted.invoiceCopyRequest.invoices) {\n  requests = invoiceCopyExtracted.invoiceCopyRequest.invoices;\n}\n\nvar i = 0;\nfor (i = 0; i < requests.length; i = i + 1) {\n  var req = requests[i] || {};\n  var trxRef = req.invoiceNumber || req.purchaseOrderNumber || req.salesOrderNumber || req.contractNumber || req.waybillNumber || req.transactionIdentifier || \"\";\n  if (trxRef !== \"\" && invalidTransactionReferences.indexOf(trxRef) === -1) {\n    invalidTransactionReferences.push(trxRef);\n  }\n}\n\nsummaryTotalInvoices = requests.length > 0 ? requests.length : 1;\nsummaryInvalidInvoiceCount = summaryTotalInvoices;\n\nsummaryErrorsByInvoice.push({\n  invoiceNumber: \"\",\n  errors: [{\n    errorCode: ERROR_CODE_TRX_NOT_IDENTIFIED,\n    errorText: ERROR_TEXT_TRX_NOT_IDENTIFIED\n  }]\n});\n\nvar result = [{\n  customer: {},\n  customerAccount: {},\n  customerSiteUse: {},\n  customerTransaction: {},\n  paymentSchedule: {},\n  businessUnit: {},\n  message: { messageId: messageId },\n  requestData: {\n    invalidTransactionReferences: invalidTransactionReferences,\n    errors: [{\n      errorCode: ERROR_CODE_TRX_NOT_IDENTIFIED,\n      errorText: ERROR_TEXT_TRX_NOT_IDENTIFIED\n    }],\n    summary: {\n      totalInvoices: summaryTotalInvoices,\n      validInvoiceCount: summaryValidInvoiceCount,\n      invalidInvoiceCount: summaryInvalidInvoiceCount,\n      amountsByCurrency: [],\n      errorsByInvoice: summaryErrorsByInvoice,\n      validTransactions: []\n    }\n  },\n  responseData: { firstRecord: \"Y\" },\n  intent: { lookupType: \"ORA_IEX_MSG_INTENT\", lookupCode: \"ORA_INVOICE_REPRINT\" },\n  processingStatus: { lookupType: \"ORA_IEX_MSG_PROCESSING_STATUS\", lookupCode: \"ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING\" }\n}];\n\nreturn result;"
          },
