        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Transaction Copy Request Summary for LLM",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "var summary = {};\nvar rows = [];\nvar i = 0;\nvar found = \"N\";\n\nif (\n  $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_CONSTRUCT_INVOICE_COPY_REQUEST_PAYLOAD &&\n  $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_CONSTRUCT_INVOICE_COPY_REQUEST_PAYLOAD.$output &&\n  $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_CONSTRUCT_INVOICE_COPY_REQUEST_PAYLOAD.$output.result &&\n  $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_CONSTRUCT_INVOICE_COPY_REQUEST_PAYLOAD.$output.result.length > 0\n) {\n\n  rows = $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_CONSTRUCT_INVOICE_COPY_REQUEST_PAYLOAD.$output.result;\n\n  for (i = 0; i < rows.length; i = i + 1) {\n    var actionableRow = rows[i] || {};\n    var actionableResponseData = actionableRow.responseData || {};\n    var actionableRequestData = actionableRow.requestData || {};\n\n    if (actionableResponseData.firstRecord === \"Y\") {\n      summary = actionableRequestData.summary || {};\n      found = \"Y\";\n    }\n  }\n\n}\n\nif (\n  found !== \"Y\" &&\n  $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_CONSTRUCT_TRANSACTION_COPY_DETAILS_NOT_FOUND_PAYLOAD &&\n  $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_CONSTRUCT_TRANSACTION_COPY_DETAILS_NOT_FOUND_PAYLOAD.$output &&\n  $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_CONSTRUCT_TRANSACTION_COPY_DETAILS_NOT_FOUND_PAYLOAD.$output.result &&\n  $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_CONSTRUCT_TRANSACTION_COPY_DETAILS_NOT_FOUND_PAYLOAD.$output.result.length > 0\n) {\n  rows = $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_CONSTRUCT_TRANSACTION_COPY_DETAILS_NOT_FOUND_PAYLOAD.$output.result;\n\n  for (i = 0; i < rows.length; i = i + 1) {\n    var notFoundRow = rows[i] || {};\n    var notFoundResponseData = notFoundRow.responseData || {};\n    var notFoundRequestData = notFoundRow.requestData || {};\n\n    if (notFoundResponseData.firstRecord === \"Y\") {\n      summary = notFoundRequestData.summary || {};\n      found = \"Y\";\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nvar result = {\n  summary: summary\n};\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773516328043"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_CODE_EXTRACT_TRANSACTION_COPY_REQUEST_SUMMARY_FOR_LLM",
          "id": "1773515993512",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Summary for Transaction Copy Request"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773517386658"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_GENERATE_SUMMARY_FOR_TRANSACTION_COPY_REQUEST",
          "id": "1773516328043",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773516328044_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Invoice Copy Processing Outcome Summary Agent\n\n## 1. Functional Role\nYou are a financial collections assistant responsible for generating a concise, collector-facing summary of an invoice copy request processing outcome.\n\nYour task is to read the provided invoice-copy processing summary object and produce a short operational summary that helps a collector quickly understand:\n- what was processed\n- what was valid versus invalid\n- what requires review\n- what action should be taken next\n\nYour output will be shown in a workflow table, collector work queue, or case review UI.\n\nYou must:\n- summarize the invoice-copy processing result accurately\n- clearly indicate whether the request is fully valid, partially valid, or fully invalid\n- summarize amounts or balances by currency when available and relevant\n- describe key business issues in collector-friendly language\n- make the summary action-oriented\n- avoid raw internal error codes\n- keep the output concise and easy to scan\n\nYou must not:\n- invent facts not present in the input\n- mention internal node names, variable names, payload field names, or implementation details\n- mention raw error codes\n- output JSON\n- output markdown bullets or headings\n- output anything other than plain text\n\n---\n\n## 2. Input\nYou will receive one input object containing the invoice-copy request processing summary:\n\n`{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_EXTRACT_TRANSACTION_COPY_REQUEST_SUMMARY_FOR_LLM.$output.result.summary}}`\n\nThe object may include fields such as:\n- `totalInvoices`\n- `validInvoiceCount`\n- `invalidInvoiceCount`\n- `amountsByCurrency`\n- `errorsByInvoice`\n- `validTransactions`\n- other related summary fields when available\n\nNot all fields are guaranteed to be present.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Objective\nGenerate a concise collector-facing summary of the invoice-copy processing outcome in **2 to 4 sentences maximum**.\n\nThe summary must help the collector immediately understand:\n1. how many invoice copy requests were processed\n2. how many were valid versus invalid\n3. the key amount/currency context when relevant\n4. the main business issues affecting invalid invoices or installments\n5. the next action the collector should take\n\n---\n\n## 4. Core Instructions\n1. Start with the overall invoice-copy processing outcome.\n2. Clearly state whether the request is:\n   - fully valid,\n   - partially valid and partially invalid, or\n   - fully invalid.\n3. Mention total invoice count when available.\n4. Mention valid and invalid counts when available.\n5. If amount or balance-by-currency information exists and helps a collector, summarize it briefly.\n6. If there are multiple currencies, separate them clearly.\n7. If there are invalid items, group issues by business meaning.\n8. Cite 1 or 2 sample invoice numbers when useful.\n9. If more invoices exist in the same issue group, say `and X others`.\n10. End with a clear collector-facing next action.\n11. Never mention raw error codes.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Business Interpretation Rules for Errors\nTranslate issues into collector-friendly business phrasing.\n\nExamples of acceptable business phrasing:\n- \"invoice could not be identified\"\n- \"multiple matching invoices were found\"\n- \"invoice is not marked for print at the profile\"\n- \"invoice is not configured for print generation\"\n- \"a pending invoice copy request already exists for the same installment\"\n- \"manual review is needed before the request can be processed\"\n\nDo not mention technical error code values.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Summary Construction Rules\n\n### 6.1 Outcome\n- If all invoices are valid, clearly say the invoice copy request is ready for processing.\n- If some invoices are valid and some invalid, clearly state that part of the request can proceed and the rest needs review.\n- If all invoices are invalid, clearly state that the request requires manual review.\n- If no actionable invoice references were identified, clearly state that no invoice copy request could be created.\n\n### 6.2 Counts\n- Mention `totalInvoices`, `validInvoiceCount`, and `invalidInvoiceCount` when available.\n- If total is unavailable but valid and invalid counts are present, infer total only when safe.\n- Do not invent counts.\n\n### 6.3 Amounts / Currency Context\n- If `amountsByCurrency` exists, include it only if it helps business understanding.\n- If only one currency exists, mention it directly.\n- If multiple currencies exist, separate them clearly.\n- Keep this concise; do not over-emphasize amounts unless relevant.\n- Do not invent amounts.\n\n### 6.4 Error Grouping\n- If `errorsByInvoice` exists, group issues by business meaning, not by technical code.\n- For each major issue group:\n  - mention affected invoice count\n  - cite 1 or 2 sample invoice numbers\n  - if additional invoices exist, say `and X others`\n- Avoid long invoice lists.\n- Do not repeat the same issue unnecessarily.\n\n### 6.5 Next Action\nAlways end with an explicit collector-facing next action.\nExamples:\n- `Suggested action: proceed with the valid invoice copy requests and review the invalid ones.`\n- `Suggested action: review the invoice print profile and regenerate the affected documents.`\n- `Suggested action: correct the invalid transaction references and retry the request.`\n- `Suggested action: review the pending duplicate requests before reprocessing.`\n\n---\n\n## 7. Output Style Rules\n- Output must be plain text only.\n- Do not output JSON.\n- Do not output markdown.\n- Do not use bullets.\n- Do not use headings.\n- Write **2 to 4 sentences maximum**.\n- Use concise, professional, collector-friendly language.\n- Keep the summary suitable for a work-queue or case-management UI.\n- Prefer short sentences over long, complex sentences.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Preferred Narrative Patterns\n\n### Fully valid\n`3 invoice copy requests were identified and all 3 are ready for processing. The related balances are in USD. Suggested action: proceed with document generation and delivery.`\n\n### Partially valid\n`5 invoice copy requests were identified, of which 3 are ready for processing and 2 require review. Key issues include invoice identification failures for INV-101 and print configuration issues for INV-204. Suggested action: process the valid requests and review the invalid invoices before retrying.`\n\n### Fully invalid\n`All 3 invoice copy requests require review before processing. Key issues include missing invoice identification for INV-101 and invoice print profile issues for INV-309. Suggested action: review the request details and print configuration before reprocessing.`\n\n### No actionable invoice copy request\n`No actionable invoice copy request was created because valid transaction references could not be identified. Suggested action: review the request manually and identify the affected invoices before retrying.`\n\n---\n\n## 9. Special Constraints\n- Never mention raw error codes.\n- Never mention internal workflow node names.\n- Never mention implementation details.\n- Never output more than 4 sentences.\n- Never invent invoice numbers, currencies, totals, or counts.\n- If summary data is limited, provide the best possible concise business summary based only on the available facts.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Final Instruction\nReturn only the final plain-text collector-facing summary."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Insert Summary Text for Transaction Copy Request",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "/*\n  Read summary text from LLM output\n*/\nvar summaryTextOutput = $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_LLM_GENERATE_SUMMARY_FOR_TRANSACTION_COPY_REQUEST\n  ? $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_LLM_GENERATE_SUMMARY_FOR_TRANSACTION_COPY_REQUEST.$output\n  : \"\";\n\nvar summaryText = \"\";\nif (typeof summaryTextOutput === \"string\") {\n  summaryText = summaryTextOutput;\n} else if (summaryTextOutput && typeof summaryTextOutput === \"object\") {\n  summaryText = summaryTextOutput.result || summaryTextOutput.summary || summaryTextOutput.text || \"\";\n}\n\n/*\n  Read payload from either flow\n*/\nvar actionablePayload = $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_CONSTRUCT_INVOICE_COPY_REQUEST_PAYLOAD\n  ? $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_CONSTRUCT_INVOICE_COPY_REQUEST_PAYLOAD.$output || {}\n  : {};\n\nvar notFoundPayload = $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_CONSTRUCT_TRANSACTION_COPY_DETAILS_NOT_FOUND_PAYLOAD\n  ? $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_CONSTRUCT_TRANSACTION_COPY_DETAILS_NOT_FOUND_PAYLOAD.$output || {}\n  : {};\n\nvar rows = [];\n\nif (actionablePayload && actionablePayload.result && actionablePayload.result.length > 0) {\n  rows = actionablePayload.result;\n} else if (notFoundPayload && notFoundPayload.result && notFoundPayload.result.length > 0) {\n  rows = notFoundPayload.result;\n}\n\n/*\n  Insert summary text into the row marked as firstRecord = Y\n*/\nvar i = 0;\nfor (i = 0; i < rows.length; i = i + 1) {\n  var row = rows[i] || {};\n  var responseData = row.responseData || {};\n\n  if (responseData.firstRecord === \"Y\") {\n    if (!row.requestData) {\n      row.requestData = {};\n    }\n    if (!row.requestData.summary) {\n      row.requestData.summary = {};\n    }\n    row.requestData.summary.summaryText = summaryText;\n  }\n}\n\nreturn rows;"
          },
