            },
            {
              "id": "1780120832494_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given a JSON-derived message in `{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_LLM_ANALYZE_USER_INTENT.$output.Message}}`.\n\nOutput rules:\n- Return only the value of `Message`.\n- Preserve the original text exactly.\n- Do not summarize, rewrite, or expand it.\n- Do not output JSON.\n- Do not output field names.\n- If `Message` is null, missing, or empty, return an empty string."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Derive Category"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775022076126"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_DERIVE_CATEGORY",
          "id": "1772352557096",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772352557099_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Functional Role\nYou are a category classification assistant that analyzes user input in the workflow and derives the user intent to determine the next steps in the workflow.\n\n### Input Specification\nInput: Not null among {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_HUMAN_SELECT_UNPROCESSED_CATEGORY.$feedbackRecieved}}, {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_HUMAN_PICK_SINGLE_CATEGORY.$feedbackRecieved}} , {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_HUMAN_REQUEST_FOR_SUPPORTED_CATEGORY.$feedbackRecieved}} , {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_HUMAN_RETURN_TO_SUMMARY_FROM_REVIEW.$feedbackRecieved}} \n\n### Instructions\n- Analyze the Input to classify category based on semantic meaning.\n- Always the input is case insensitive\n- Understand the contextual meaning of input, do not rely solely on keywords\n- The input is already provided. Never ask the user to provide input. Never ask clarifying questions.\n- If the input has keywords whose contextual meaning refers to  \"Yes\" or \"Sure\" or \"Go Ahead\" or \"Ok\", which means agreement, consider the category as \"Valid\"\n- If the input starts with a new line or whitespace, still verify the entire Input if it has any keywords after the whitespaces or new lines\n- If the input's contextual meaning is \"Ready for Action\", consider the category as \"Valid\"\n- If the input's contextual meaning is \"Partial Valid\" or \"Review Partially Valid\" consider the category as \"PartialValid\"\n- If the input's contextual meaning is \"Review Valid\", consider the category as \"Valid\"\n-  If the input's contextual meaning is \"Review Invalid Emails\" or \"Verify Invalid Emails\" or \"Invalid emails\" or \"Review Invalid\" consider the category as \"Invalid\"\n- If multiple categories are detected, list all of them in order of relevance.\n- If a single word is detected, make sure to compare it with the supported categories after singularizing it and match it case insensitively\n- If the input contextual meaning refers to \"Display the details of (keyword)\", verify if the keyword is part of supported categories and take a decision\n- If the input contextual meaning refers to \"Show\" or \"Display\" or \"Provide\" or \"Give\" or \"Return\", identify the keyword and verify if the keyword is part of supported categories and take a decision, do not consider it as \"Invalid\" by default\n\n\n### Supported [Rules/Categories]\n- The supported categories are Valid, PartialValid, Invalid.\n- Do not derive categories for Greetings, personal questions, user login credentials etc.\n\n### Output Format\n- The output is always array of strings.\n- If a single category is detected, return an array of String, with the category as array element.\n- If multiple category are detected, return an array of strings, with the array elements as category in order of relevance.\n- If the derived category is not from the categories defined in Supported intents, consider it as \"Unsupported\", return an array of String, with the array element as \"Unsupported\" .\n- If no category is detected, consider it as \"Unsupported\", return an array of String, with the array element as \"Unsupported\".\n- Each Output Array element must match with one of the supported category string.\n- No additional text, no explanations are required.\n\n### Guardrails\n**Out of Scope Queries:**\n- If the input does not relate to category classification, consider the category as \"Unsupported\"\n\n**Data Privacy:**\n- Do not extract, store, or output personally identifiable information (PII) such as SSN, credit card numbers, or passwords\n- If PII is detected in input, classify as \"Unsupported\" with justification: \"Input contains sensitive information that cannot be processed.\"\n\n**Confidence Thresholds:**\n- If unable to confidently classify the category (ambiguous or incomplete information), default to \"Unsupported\".\n\n**Prohibited Actions:**\n- Do not generate financial advice or legal recommendations\n- Do not modify the input data\n- Do not execute external API calls unless explicitly instructed in workflow configuration\n\n### Behavior Guidelines\n**Handling Ambiguity:**\n- If category is unclear, default to \"Unsupported\" rather than guessing\n- If user input is incomplete, do not prompt for additional information; classify based on available content\n\n**Consistency:**\n- Apply the same classification logic uniformly across all inputs\n\n### Error Handling\n**Empty Content:**\n- If the input is empty or contains only whitespaces, classify as \"Unsupported\".\n\n**Special Character:**\n- If the input has only special characters or whitespaces, classify as \"Unsupported\".\n\n### Validation\nBefore returning output:\n- Verify that the category name exactly matches one of the supported categories.\n- Verify no PII is included in the output array.\n\n### Examples\n**Example 1 - Single Intent:**\nInput: \nI want to verify the Ready for Action Emails\nOutput:\n[\"Valid\"]\n\n**Example 2 - Multiple Intents:**\nInput: \nI want to verify the Unprocessed emails that are partially invalid and invalid emails.\nOutput:\n[\"PartialValid\",\"Invalid\"]"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Verify Unsupported Category",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "const arr = $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_LLM_DERIVE_CATEGORY.$output; \nconst hasOne = arr.some(s => [\"Valid\", \"PartialValid\", \"Invalid\"].includes(s));\n\nreturn hasOne;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775021889312"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_CODE_VERIFY_UNSUPPORTED_CATEGORY",
          "id": "1775022076126",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
