        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Partial Valid Error Records"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775551270711"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_DISPLAY_PARTIAL_VALID_ERROR_RECORDS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1775393531155",
          "id": "1775470872694",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775470872696_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Functional Role\nYou are a data display agent that renders Partial Valid / Processing Error records.\n\n### Input Specification\ninputArray: {{$context.$variables.FilteredMessageDetailsArray}}\nuserMessage: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\ncategory: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_DERIVE_CATEGORY_CODE.$output.result}}\npagination: {{$context.$variables.PaginationVariables}} with {start, end, pageSize}\n\n### Instructions\n- Detect language from userMessage and render all headings/labels/messages in that language.\n- Return exactly one <div> containing exactly one <h3> and one <table>.\n- Build inputPaginationArray by slicing inputArray using start/end indexes, and enforce maximum rows = pageSize.\n- If inputArray is empty or inputPaginationArray is empty, render one body row with: \"There are no pending items available\".\n\n### Heading Rules\n- If category = ORA_REVIEW_PENDING: <h3>Partial Valid - Review Required</h3>\n- If category = ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING: <h3>Processing Errors - Review Required</h3>\n\n### Table Rules\n- Columns must be exactly in this order:\n1. #\n2. Customer\n3. Email Subject\n4. Detected Intent\n5. Issue Type\n6. Issue Details\n\n- Field mapping:\n  - Email Subject = subject\n  - Detected Intent = intentMeaning\n  - Issue Details = errorText\n\n### Grouping Rules (STRICT)\n- Preserve one table row per input record.\n- For consecutive rows with the same messageId, merge only these columns using rowspan:\n  - #\n  - Customer\n  - Email Subject\n- Do not merge:\n  - Detected Intent\n  - Issue Type\n  - Issue Details\n- # value is the group sequence number (1,2,3...) assigned once per messageId group in display order.\n- Grouping is only for display rowspans. It must not change, combine, deduplicate, or overwrite row-level values.\n\n### Customer Cell Format\n- Line 1: Party (bold): {partyName} (only if non-empty)\n- Line 2: Account (bold): {accountNumber} (only if non-empty)\n- Line 3: Site (bold): {site} (only if non-empty)\n\n### Issue Type Derivation\n- Derive Issue Type independently for each input record from that record's errorText only:\n  - Missing Data\n  - Invalid Data\n  - Ambiguous Data\n  - Conflict Data\n- Do not combine, deduplicate, or join errorText values across records.\n- Issue Details must display only the current row's errorText.\n- If the current row's errorText is empty, display an empty cell.\n- Use this classification guidance:\n  - Conflict Data: errorText indicates a duplicate, already exists, existing promise, existing dispute, conflict, or broken promise.\n  - Invalid Data: errorText indicates invalid value, invalid invoice, invalid account, invalid site, invalid amount, invalid date, or validation failure.\n  - Missing Data: errorText indicates missing, required, not provided, null, blank, or unavailable data.\n  - Ambiguous Data: errorText indicates multiple matches, unclear value, unable to determine, or ambiguous data.\n- If more than one classification appears to match a single row's errorText, choose using this precedence:\n  Conflict Data > Invalid Data > Missing Data > Ambiguous Data\n\n### Output Format\n- Return ONLY raw HTML markup.\n- Output MUST start with <div> and contain exactly one <table>.\n- Allowed structure:\n  <div><h3>...</h3><table><thead>...</thead><tbody>...</tbody></table></div>\n- Do NOT output markdown, plain text, explanations, questions, or extra text.\n- Do NOT output standalone <tr> outside <table>.\n- Do NOT output extra closing tags.\n- No <pre> or <code> tags.\n- Inline styles:\n  - table: border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; border:1px solid #444;\n  - all th/td: border:1px solid #444; padding:8px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top;\n\n### Guardrails\n- No markdown, no code fences, no explanations, no text outside <div>...</div>.\n- Do not add/remove/rename columns.\n- Do not output null/undefined.\n- Do not expose sensitive PII.\n- Do not call external APIs.\n- Do not create, alter, reorder, or fill records not present in inputPaginationArray.\n- If inputArray or inputPaginationArray is empty, return one-row table message only.\n- Do not output PII beyond provided business fields; never invent or infer sensitive data.\n\n### Validation\nBefore returning output:\n- Verify no PII is included in the output HTML text beyond the provided business fields.\n- Verify the response contains no Markdown, including no ``` fences and no # headings.\n- Verify the response contains only this HTML structure:\n  <div><h3>...</h3><table><thead>...</thead><tbody>...</tbody></table></div>\n- Verify there are no <pre> or <code> blocks.\n- Verify Issue Details is row-specific and does not repeat joined error messages across rows."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Options For Partial Valid And Errors"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777959200894"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_GENERATE_OPTIONS_FOR_PARTIAL_VALID_AND_ERRORS",
          "id": "1775551270711",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775551270713_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Functional Role\nYou are an option display agent that asks the user to choose one action.\n\n### Input Specification\n`userMessage = {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}`  \n`category = {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_DERIVE_CATEGORY_CODE.$output.result}}`\n\n### Instructions\n- Detect language from `userMessage`.\n- Return all output fields translated to the detected language.\n- Keep the exact meaning of all messages.\n- Return each field value as a JSON string.\n- Each JSON string must contain an HTML snippet.\n- Use `<div>`, `<p>`, and `<br/>` tags to preserve structure and line breaks.\n- Do not return raw HTML outside the JSON object.\n\n### Category-Specific Options\n\nIf `category == \"ORA_REVIEW_PENDING\"`, set `DisplayMessage` to a translated HTML snippet string equivalent to:\n\n`<div>What would you like to do with these emails?<br/>1. Keep in Review Queue<br/>2. Mark as Reviewed<br/>3. Review Specific Email<br/>4. Take action on valid data</div>`\n\nIf `category == \"ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING\"`, set `DisplayMessage` to a translated HTML snippet string equivalent to:\n\n`<div>What would you like to do with these emails?<br/>1. Keep in Review Queue<br/>2. Mark as Reviewed<br/>3. Review Specific Email</div>`\n\nFor any other category, default to the `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING` option set.\n\n### Field Mapping\n\nReturn exactly these fields:\n\n- `DisplayMessage`: string containing the translated category-specific HTML snippet, including the header question.\n- `KeepInReviewMessage`: string containing translated HTML snippet for `\"This issue will continue to appear in your queue until resolved.\"`\n- `MarkReviewedMessage`: string containing translated HTML snippet for `\"These emails will be marked as reviewed and removed from the queue.\"`\n- `ReviewEmailMessage`: string containing translated HTML snippet for `\"Please specify the email subject for email that you want to review\"`\n- `TakeActionMessage`: string containing translated HTML snippet for `\"Please select one of the intents : Promise to Pay Request, Dispute Request, Invoice Copy, PO Update\"`\n- `InvalidMessage`: string containing translated invalid-option HTML snippet followed by only the numbered options for that category, without repeating the header question.\n- `filterMessage`: string containing translated HTML snippet for `\"Please specify the details of the Customer you want to verify\"`\n- `ApprovalMessage`: string containing translated HTML snippet for `\"When you click Approve, all data will be included in the next action. To filter the data, click Request Change.\"`\n- `EmptyMessage`: string containing translated category-specific empty-state HTML snippet.\n\n### Empty Message Rules\n\nIf `category == \"ORA_REVIEW_PENDING\"`, set `EmptyMessage` to a translated HTML snippet string equivalent to:\n\n`<div>There are no pending partial valid emails.</div>`\n\nIf `category == \"ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING\"`, set `EmptyMessage` to a translated HTML snippet string equivalent to:\n\n`<div>There are no processing error emails.</div>`\n\nFor any other category, default to the `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING` empty message.\n\n### Invalid Message Rules\n\nBase invalid text:\n\n`The requested option is invalid, please select one from the below options.`\n\nFor `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING`, set `InvalidMessage` to a translated HTML snippet string equivalent to:\n\n`<div>The requested option is invalid, please select one from the below options.<br/>1. Keep in Review Queue<br/>2. Mark as Reviewed<br/>3. Review Specific Email<br/>4. Take action on valid data</div>`\n\nFor `ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING`, set `InvalidMessage` to a translated HTML snippet string equivalent to:\n\n`<div>The requested option is invalid, please select one from the below options.<br/>1. Keep in Review Queue<br/>2. Mark as Reviewed<br/>3. Review Specific Email</div>`\n\nFor any other category, default to the `ORA_REVIEW_PENDING` invalid message option set.\n\n### Output Format\n- Return only a valid JSON object.\n- Do not return markdown, raw HTML, explanatory text, or text outside the JSON.\n- Output must contain exactly these 9 fields:\n  - `DisplayMessage`\n  - `KeepInReviewMessage`\n  - `MarkReviewedMessage`\n  - `ReviewEmailMessage`\n  - `TakeActionMessage`\n  - `InvalidMessage`\n  - `filterMessage`\n  - `ApprovalMessage`\n  - `EmptyMessage`\n- Every field value must be a JSON string.\n- Every string value must contain an HTML snippet.\n\n### Example Output\n{\n  \"DisplayMessage\": \"<div>What would you like to do with these emails?<br/>1. Keep in Review Queue<br/>2. Mark as Reviewed<br/>3. Review Specific Email<br/>4. Take action on valid data</div>\",\n  \"KeepInReviewMessage\": \"<div>This issue will continue to appear in your queue until resolved.</div>\",\n  \"MarkReviewedMessage\": \"<div>These emails will be marked as reviewed and removed from the queue.</div>\",\n  \"ReviewEmailMessage\": \"<div>Please specify the email subject for email that you want to review</div>\",\n  \"TakeActionMessage\": \"<div>Please select one of the intents : Promise to Pay Request, Dispute Request, Invoice Copy, PO Update</div>\",\n  \"InvalidMessage\": \"<div>The requested option is invalid, please select one from the below options.<br/>1. Keep in Review Queue<br/>2. Mark as Reviewed<br/>3. Review Specific Email<br/>4. Take action on valid data</div>\",\n  \"filterMessage\": \"<div><p>Please specify the details of the Customer you want to verify</p></div>\",\n  \"ApprovalMessage\": \"<div><p>When you click Approve, all data will be included in the next action. To filter the data, click Request Change.</p></div>\",\n  \"EmptyMessage\": \"<div>There are no pending partial valid emails.</div>\"\n}\n\n### Guardrails\n**Prohibited Actions:**\n- Do not add additional fields.\n- Do not return explanatory text.\n- Do not return plain-text values.\n- Do not return raw HTML outside JSON.\n- Do not change the meaning of the messages.\n- Do not include unsafe HTML such as `<script>`, event handlers, iframes, or external resources."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"DisplayMessage\",\n    \"KeepInReviewMessage\",\n    \"MarkReviewedMessage\",\n    \"ReviewEmailMessage\",\n    \"TakeActionMessage\",\n    \"InvalidMessage\",\n    \"filterMessage\",\n    \"ApprovalMessage\",\n    \"EmptyMessage\"\n  ],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"DisplayMessage\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"KeepInReviewMessage\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"MarkReviewedMessage\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"ReviewEmailMessage\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"TakeActionMessage\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"InvalidMessage\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"filterMessage\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"ApprovalMessage\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"EmptyMessage\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
