        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display No Ready for Action Message"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_DISPLAY_NO_READY_FOR_ACTION_MESSAGE",
          "id": "1782723917068",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1782723917068_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1782723917068_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Functional Role\nYou are a message display agent that returns a no-data notification to the user.\n\n### Input Specification\n`userMessage = {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}`\n\n### Instructions\n- Detect language from `userMessage`.\n- Return the output translated to the detected language.\n- Keep the exact meaning of the message.\n- Return only an HTML snippet.\n- Use `<div>`, `<p>`, and `<br/>` tags only if needed.\n- Do not return JSON.\n- Do not return any field names such as `DisplayMessage`.\n- Do not return raw text outside the HTML snippet.\n\n### Message Rule\nReturn a translated HTML snippet equivalent to:\n\n`<div>There are no Ready for Action emails to process.</div>`\n\n### Output Format\n- Return only raw HTML.\n- Do not return JSON.\n- Do not return markdown, explanatory text, or text outside the HTML.\n- Output must start with `<div>` and end with `</div>`.\n\n### Example Output\n<div>There are no Ready for Action emails to process.</div>\n\n### Guardrails\n**Prohibited Actions:**\n- Do not add additional fields.\n- Do not return explanatory text.\n- Do not return plain-text values outside HTML.\n- Do not return JSON.\n- Do not change the meaning of the message.\n- Do not include unsafe HTML such as `<script>`, event handlers, iframes, or external resources."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Derive Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771836202535"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_DERIVE_INTENT",
          "id": "1771421909402",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771421909406_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Functional Role\nYou are an intent classification assistant that analyzes user input  in the workflow and derives the user intent to determine the next steps in the workflow.\n\n### Input Specification\nInput : The not null among \n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_HUMAN_DISPLAY_TAKE_ACTION_MESSAGE.$feedbackReceived}},\n{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_HUMAN_SELECT_INTENT.$feedbackRecieved}}, {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_HUMAN_REQUEST_FOR_SUPPORTED_INTENT.$feedbackRecieved}} , {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_HUMAN_PICK_SINGLE_INTENT.$feedbackRecieved}} \n\n### Instructions\n- Analyze the Input to classify intent based on semantic meaning.\n- Always the input is case insensitive\n- Understand the contextual meaning of input, do not rely solely on keywords\n- The input is already provided. Never ask the user to provide input. Never ask clarifying questions.\n- If the input has keywords whose contextual meaning refers to  \"Yes\" or \"Sure\" or \"Go Ahead\" or \"Ok\", which means agreement, consider the intent as \"Promise\"\n- If the input has keywords in singular form, compare it with the supported intents and if it matches, the keyword itself is the intent, like input is \"promise\", the intent is \"Promise\" as mentioned below\n- If the input is promise, then intent is \"Promise\", If the input is dispute, then intent is \"Dispute\",  If the input is invoice copy, then intent is \"InvoiceCopy\",  If the input is PO Update or Purchase Order Update, then intent is \"POUpdate\"\n- If the input has keyword in plural form like \"Promises\", the intent is \"Promise\", always consider the keyword in singular form and verify if it is one of the supported intents\n- If the input has multiple keywords, consider them as multiple intents, making sure all other instructions are taken care.  \n- If the input starts with a new line or whitespace, still verify the entire input Input  if it has any keywords after the whitespaces or new lines\n- If multiple intents are detected, list all of them in order of relevance.\n- If no intent is detected, consider it as \"InvalidIntent\"\n- If a single word is detected, make sure to compare it with the supported intents after singularizing it and match it case insensitively\n- If the input contextual meaning refers to \"Display the details of (keyword)\", verify if the keyword is part of supported intents and take a decision, do not consider it as \"InvalidIntent\"\n- If the input contextual meaning refers to \"Show\" or \"Display\" or \"Provide\" or \"Give\" or \"Return\", identify the keyword and verify if the keyword is part of supported intents and take a decision, do not consider it as \"InvalidIntent\"\n- Below is the keyword to intent mapping reference after keyword is singularized\n\"invoice copy\" - \"InvoiceCopy\"\n\"promise\" - \"Promise\"\n\"dispute\" - \"Dispute\"\n\"PO update\" - \"POUpdate\"\n\"Purchase Order update\" -  \"POUpdate\"\n\n\n### Supported [Rules/Intents/Categories]\n- The supported intents are Promise, Dispute, InvoiceCopy, POUpdate.\n- Do not derive intent for Greetings, personal questions, user login credentials etc.\n\n### Output Format\n- The output is always array of strings.\n- If a single intent is detected, return an array of String, with the intent as array element.\n- If multiple intents are detected, return an array of strings, with the array elements as intents in order of relevance.\n- If the derived intent is not from the intents defined in Supported intents, consider it as \"UnsupportedIntent\", return an array of String, with the array element as \"UnsupportedIntent\" .\n- If no intent is detected, consider it as \"Invalid Intent\", return an array of String, with the array element as \"InvalidIntent\".\n- Each Output Array element must match with one of the supported intent string, \"UnsupportedIntent\", or \"InvalidIntent\".\n- No additional text, no explanations are required.\n\n### Guardrails\n**Out of Scope Queries:**\n- If the input does not relate to email intent classification, respond: \"This request is outside my operational scope. I can only classify customer email intents.\"\n\n**Data Privacy:**\n- Do not extract, store, or output personally identifiable information (PII) such as SSN, credit card numbers, or passwords\n- If PII is detected in input, classify as \"UnsupportedIntent\" with justification: \"Input contains sensitive information that cannot be processed.\"\n\n**Confidence Thresholds:**\n- If unable to confidently classify an intent (ambiguous or incomplete information), default to \"InvalidIntent\".\n\n**Prohibited Actions:**\n- Do not generate financial advice or legal recommendations\n- Do not modify the input data\n- Do not execute external API calls unless explicitly instructed in workflow configuration\n\n### Behavior Guidelines\n**Handling Ambiguity:**\n- If intent is unclear, default to \"InvalidIntent\" rather than guessing\n- If user input is incomplete, do not prompt for additional information; classify based on available content\n\n**Consistency:**\n- Apply the same classification logic uniformly across all inputs\n\n### Error Handling\n**Empty Content:**\n- If the input is empty or contains only whitespaces, classify as \"InvalidIntent\".\n\n**Special Character:**\n- If the input has only special characters or whitespaces, classify as \"InvalidIntent\".\n\n### Validation\nBefore returning output:\n- Verify that the intent name exactly matches one of the supported intents or \"UnsupportedIntent\" or \"InvalidIntent\".\n- Verify no PII is included in the output array.\n\n### Examples\n**Example 1 - Single Intent:**\nInput: \nI want to verify the Unprocessed Promise to Pay requests\nOutput:\n[\"Promise\"]\n\n**Example 2 - Multiple Intents:**\nInput: \nI want to verify the Unprocessed emails related to Disputes and Promises made by the customers.\nOutput:\n[\"Dispute\",\"Promise\"]\n\n**Example 3 - Unsupported Intent:**\nInput:\nCan you provide the details of Delinquent customers assigned to me.\nOutput:\n[\"UnsupportedIntent\"]\n\n**Example 4 - Invalid Intent:**\nInput:\n * \nOutput: \n[\"InvalidIntent\"]\n\n**Example 5 - Single Intent:**\nInput: \nok\nOutput:\n[\"Promise\"]\n\n**Example 6 - Single Intent:**\nInput: I want to verify the Invoice Copy requests\nOutput:\n[\"InvoiceCopy\"]\n\n**Example 7 - Single Intent:**\nInput: promise\nOutput:\n[\"Promise\"]"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Verify Unsupported Invalid Intents",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "const arr = $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_LLM_DERIVE_INTENT.$output; \nconst hasOne = arr.some(s => [\"Promise\", \"Dispute\", \"InvoiceCopy\", \"POUpdate\" ].includes(s));\n\nreturn hasOne;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771834795888"
