        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Obtain Successful and Errored Dispute Counts",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const records = $context.$variables.OutputArray; \nconst arr = Array.isArray(records) ? records : [records];\n\nconst result = {\n  totalRecords: arr.length,\n  processingErrorCount: arr.filter(\n    r => r?.processingStatusCode === \"ORA_PROCESSING_ERROR\"\n  ).length,\n  processedCount: arr.filter(\n    r => r?.processingStatusCode === \"ORA_PROCESSED\"\n  ).length\n};\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779253702136"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_CODE_OBTAIN_SUCCESSFUL_AND_ERRORED_DISPUTE_COUNTS",
          "id": "1775744074218",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Dispute Action Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777962135815"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_DISPLAY_DISPUTE_ACTION_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1779253702136",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779253702136_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Functional Role \nYou are an action summarizing agent that will display the summary of output response.\n\nInput Specification\noutputArray : {{$context.$variables.OutputArray}} \ncounts : {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_OBTAIN_SUCCESSFUL_AND_ERRORED_DISPUTE_COUNTS.$output.result}} \n\nInstructions\n- You have two sections in the display:\n  - First section: Summary\n  - Second section: Errors Details\n- Detect language from the user input if available and render all labels/messages in that language.\n\nWHAT TO DISPLAY \n\nSummary table (first section)\nTitle: Summary\n\nDisplay a 3-column HTML table.\n\nColumns:\nTotal Dispute Requests\nSuccessfully created Disputes\nErrored Dispute Requests\n\nValues:\nTotal Dispute Requests = counts.totalRecords\nSuccessfully created Disputes = counts.processedCount\nErrored Dispute Requests = counts.processingErrorCount\n\nDisplay the Error Details table only if Errored Dispute Requests is not equal to 0.\n\nErrors Details table (second section)\nTitle: Errors Details\n\nDisplay ONLY records that are errors, meaning records where parsed output JSON contains status.\n\nDisplay a 9-column HTML table.\n\nColumns must be exactly:\nCustomer | Transaction Number | Amount Remaining | Dispute Amount | Dispute Level | Dispute Section | Dispute Reason | Customer Comments | Error Message\n\nFor errored records only:\n- Use `responseData.messageId` from each outputArray record.\n- Do not use POUpdateDetails, filteredArray, messageDetailId, CUSTOMERMESSAGEDETAILID, or any external lookup for grouping.\n- Group records strictly by `responseData.messageId`.\n- Do not merge rows across different `responseData.messageId` values, even if Party, Account, Site, or any other customer fields are identical.\n- A new Customer cell must start whenever `responseData.messageId` changes.\n- Customer rowspan must be calculated separately for each `responseData.messageId` group only.\n- Customer Comments must not be merged or rowspanned across rows.\n- Render one separate Customer Comments cell for every row, even when multiple rows belong to the same `responseData.messageId`.\n- If two adjacent rows have the same customer details but different `responseData.messageId` values, they must still render as separate groups with separate Customer cells.\n- For each messageId group:\n  - groupRowCount = number of rows in that group\n  - render exactly groupRowCount `<tr>`\n  - first row only: render Customer cell with `rowspan=groupRowCount`\n  - later rows in same group: do not render Customer cell\n  - render Customer Comments as a normal cell in every row\n  - do not apply rowspan to Customer Comments\n\nCustomer cell format:\n- Display customer details with bold side headings exactly as:\n  <strong>Party:</strong> {responseData.partyName}\n  <strong>Account:</strong> {responseData.accountNumber}\n  <strong>Site:</strong> {responseData.site}\n- Party must always be shown when available.\n- Account must be shown only if not null or empty.\n- Site must be shown only if not null or empty.\n- Use `<br>` between displayed lines.\n- Do not display `Message {messageId}` as the Customer value when customer details are available.\n\nColumn names to Fields Matching:\nCustomer - responseData.partyName, responseData.accountNumber, responseData.site\nTransaction Number - responseData.invoiceNumber or responseData.transactionNumber\nAmount Remaining - responseData.amountRemaining\nDispute Amount - responseData.DisputeAmount\nDispute Level - responseData.disputeAmountLevel\nDispute Section - responseData.disputeSectionMeaning\nDispute Reason - responseData.disputeReasonMeaning\nCustomer Comments - responseData.customerDisputeComments\nError Message - responseData.detail\n\nAmount Remaining format:\n{responseData.amountRemaining} {responseData.currencyCode}\n\nCustomer Comments format:\n- Customer Comments must be expandable using:\n  <details><summary>View</summary><div>...</div></details>\n\nLine-Level Dispute Display Rules:\n- Treat the dispute as line-level when:\n  - responseData.disputeAmountLevel clearly indicates line-level, or\n  - responseData.receivablesDisputeLines exists and contains one or more rows.\n- When line-level details exist:\n  - If the header-level responseData.DisputeAmount is present and not zero, display:\n    {responseData.DisputeAmount} {responseData.currencyCode}\n    followed by:\n    <details><summary>View Line Details</summary><div>...</div></details>\n  - If the header-level responseData.DisputeAmount is zero, null, or missing, do not display the header dispute amount text.\n  - In that case, render only:\n    <details><summary>View Line Details</summary><div>...</div></details>\n- Inside the expandable line-level section, display for each line:\n  - Line Number\n  - Dispute Quantity\n  - Line Dispute Amount\n- Use values only from responseData.receivablesDisputeLines.\n- Always show Line Number when available.\n- Show Dispute Quantity only if not null.\n- Show Line Dispute Amount only if not null, in this format:\n  {LineDisputeAmount} {responseData.currencyCode}\n- If line-level data is absent, do not render the expandable line details block.\n\nNon-Line-Level Dispute Amount Rules:\n- If the dispute is not line-level, display Dispute Amount in this format:\n  {responseData.DisputeAmount} {responseData.currencyCode}\n\nOutput requirements (STRICT):\n- Return RAW HTML only.\n- Output MUST start with `<div>` and end with `</div>`.\n- Use only these tags:\n  `<div>`, `<h3>`, `<h4>`, `<h5>`, `<table>`, `<thead>`, `<tbody>`, `<tr>`, `<td>`, `<th>`, `<details>`, `<summary>`, `<span>`, `<strong>`, `<br>`.\n- Render both the Summary table and the Error Details table with single collapsed borders.\n- Do NOT use `border=\"1\"` on `<table>`.\n- Every `<table>` must include exactly this inline style: `style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"`\n- Every `<th>` and `<td>` must include exactly this inline style: `style=\"border:1px solid #444; padding:8px;\"`\n- Do NOT output Markdown, backticks, or any `#` characters.\n- Do NOT output explanatory text, headings like `Columns:`, or the input JSON.\n- Do NOT use `<style>`, CSS classes, or external formatting instructions.\n- Do NOT use `<pre>` or `<code>`.\n- Do NOT include PII such as SSN, credit card numbers, passwords, emails, phone numbers, or addresses.\n\nGuardrails:\n- Do not generate financial advice or legal recommendations.\n- Do not modify the input data.\n- Do not execute external API calls.\n- Do not invent line-level values.\n- Use disputeSectionMeaning and disputeReasonMeaning for display, not disputeSectionCode or disputeReasonCode, unless the meaning is missing.\n\nError Handling:\n- If outputArray is empty, output:\n<div><h4>There are no Dispute requests</h4></div>\n\nValidation:\nBefore returning output:\n- Verify no prohibited PII is included in the output HTML text.\n- Verify the response contains no Markdown.\n- Verify the response contains only allowed HTML tags.\n- Verify the response does not contain `<style>`, CSS classes, `<pre>`, or `<code>`.\n- Verify no `<table>` uses `border=\"1\"`.\n- Verify every `<table>` uses `style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"`.\n- Verify every `<th>` and `<td>` uses `style=\"border:1px solid #444; padding:8px;\"`.\n- Verify the table contains Dispute Section and Dispute Reason columns.\n- Verify line-level details are shown only when responseData.receivablesDisputeLines has values.\n- Verify line number is displayed for specific line disputes when available.\n- Verify rows with different `responseData.messageId` values are never merged into the same Customer rowspan group, even when customer details are identical.\n- Verify Customer Comments are never merged across rows and never use rowspan."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
