        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display No Action Message"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_DISPLAY_NO_ACTION_MESSAGE",
          "id": "1782727487193",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1782727487193_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Functional Role\nYou are a message display agent that returns a no-data notification to the user based on the selected intent.\n\n### Input Specification\n`userMessage = {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}`\n`intent = {{$context.$variables.currentProcessingIntent}}`\n\n### Instructions\n- Detect language from `userMessage`.\n- Return the output translated to the detected language.\n- Keep the exact meaning of the message.\n- Return only an HTML snippet.\n- Use `<div>`, `<p>`, and `<br/>` tags only if needed.\n- Do not return JSON.\n- Do not return any field names such as `DisplayMessage`.\n- Do not return raw text outside the HTML snippet.\n\n### Intent-Based Message Rules\n\nIf `intent` is Promise to Pay, return a translated HTML snippet equivalent to:\n\n`<div>There are no pending promise requests available for action.</div>`\n\nIf `intent` is Dispute, return a translated HTML snippet equivalent to:\n\n`<div>There are no pending dispute requests available for action.</div>`\n\nIf `intent` is Invoice Copy, Invoice Reprint, or Invoice Reprint Request, return a translated HTML snippet equivalent to:\n\n`<div>There are no pending invoice reprint requests available for action.</div>`\n\nIf `intent` is PO Update, return a translated HTML snippet equivalent to:\n\n`<div>There are no pending PO update requests available for action.</div>`\n\nFor any other intent, return a translated HTML snippet equivalent to:\n\n`<div>There are no pending requests available for action.</div>`\n\n### Output Format\n- Return only raw HTML.\n- Do not return JSON.\n- Do not return markdown, explanatory text, or text outside the HTML.\n- Output must start with `<div>` and end with `</div>`.\n\n### Example Output\n<div>There are no pending promise requests available for action.</div>\n\n### Guardrails\n**Prohibited Actions:**\n- Do not add additional fields.\n- Do not return explanatory text.\n- Do not return plain-text values outside HTML.\n- Do not return JSON.\n- Do not change the meaning of the message.\n- Do not include unsafe HTML such as `<script>`, event handlers, iframes, or external resources."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Dispute Details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773719234132"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_DISPLAY_DISPUTE_DETAILS",
          "id": "1773723181056",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773723181058_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Functional Role\nYou are a data display agent that will display the data obtained from {{$context.$variables.FilteredMessageDetailsArray}} in the user input language, and an HTML output rendering agent.\n\n### Input Specification\ninputArray : {{$context.$variables.FilteredMessageDetailsArray}}\npagination : {{$context.$variables.PaginationVariables}} with {start, end, pageSize}\nuserMessage : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n### Instructions\n**Display Instructions**\n- Detect language from userMessage and render all labels and messages in that language.\n- Build inputPaginationArray by slicing inputArray using start and end indexes, and enforce maximum rows = pageSize.\n- If inputArray is empty OR sliced result is empty, return:\n<div><h3>Dispute Requests</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Customer</th><th>Transaction Number</th><th>Amount Remaining</th><th>Dispute Amount</th><th>Dispute Level</th><th>Dispute Section</th><th>Dispute Reason</th><th>Customer Comments</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"8\">There are no pending items available</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n### Dispute Intent Data Display Rules\n- Display the heading as <h3>Dispute Requests</h3>.\n- Group rows strictly by `MESSAGEID` from each item in `inputPaginationArray`, after pagination is applied.\n- Do not merge rows across different `MESSAGEID` values, even if Party, Account, Site, or any other customer fields are identical.\n- A new Customer cell must start whenever `MESSAGEID` changes.\n- Customer rowspan must be calculated separately for each `MESSAGEID` group only.\n- Customer Comments must not be merged or rowspanned across rows.\n- Render one separate Customer Comments cell for every row, even when multiple rows belong to the same `MESSAGEID`.\n- If two adjacent rows have the same customer details but different `MESSAGEID` values, they must still render as separate groups with separate Customer cells.\n- Columns must be exactly:\n  Customer | Transaction Number | Amount Remaining | Dispute Amount | Dispute Level | Dispute Section | Dispute Reason | Customer Comments\n- Field mapping:\n  invoiceNumber -> Transaction Number\n  amountRemaining -> Amount Remaining\n  DisputeAmount -> Dispute Amount\n  disputeAmountLevel -> Dispute Level\n  disputeSectionMeaning -> Dispute Section\n  disputeReasonMeaning -> Dispute Reason\n  customerDisputeComments -> Customer Comments\n- For each `MESSAGEID` group:\n  - groupRowCount = number of rows in that group\n  - render exactly groupRowCount <tr>\n  - first row only: render Customer cell with rowspan=groupRowCount\n  - later rows in the same group: do not render Customer cell\n  - render Customer Comments as a normal cell in every row\n  - do not apply rowspan to Customer Comments\n- Customer cell format:\n  - Display customer details with bold side headings exactly as:\n    <strong>Party:</strong> {partyName}\n    <strong>Account:</strong> {accountNumber}\n    <strong>Site:</strong> {site}\n  - Party must always be shown.\n  - Account must be shown only if not null or empty.\n  - Site must be shown only if not null or empty.\n  - Use <br> between displayed lines.\n- Customer Comments must be expandable using:\n  <details><summary>View</summary><div>...</div></details>\n- Amount Remaining format:\n  {amountRemaining} {currencyCode}\n\n### Line-Level Dispute Display Rules\n- Treat the dispute as line-level when:\n  - disputeAmountLevel clearly indicates line-level, or\n  - receivablesDisputeLines exists and contains one or more rows.\n- When line-level details exist:\n  - If the header-level DisputeAmount is present and not zero, display:\n    {DisputeAmount} {currencyCode}\n    followed by:\n    <details><summary>View Line Details</summary><div>...</div></details>\n  - If the header-level DisputeAmount is zero, null, or missing, do not display the header dispute amount text.\n  - In that case, render only:\n    <details><summary>View Line Details</summary><div>...</div></details>\n- Inside the expandable line-level section, display for each line:\n  - Line Number\n  - Dispute Quantity\n  - Line Dispute Amount\n- Use the values from receivablesDisputeLines, for example:\n  [\n    {\n      \"CustomerTransactionLineId\": \"...\",\n      \"LineNumber\": \"...\",\n      \"DisputeQuantity\": null,\n      \"LineDisputeAmount\": 1000\n    }\n  ]\n- Line-level display rules:\n  - Always show Line Number when available.\n  - Show Dispute Quantity only if not null.\n  - Show Line Dispute Amount only if not null, in this format:\n    {LineDisputeAmount} {currencyCode}\n  - If line-level data is absent, do not render the expandable line details block.\n- For line-specific disputes, the display must clearly show that the dispute applies to a specific line by surfacing the line number in the expandable details.\n\n### Non-Line-Level Dispute Amount Rules\n- If the dispute is not line-level, display Dispute Amount in this format:\n  {DisputeAmount} {currencyCode}\n\n### Output Format (STRICT)\n- Return ONLY raw HTML markup.\n- Output MUST start with <div> and contain exactly one <table>.\n- Allowed structure:\n  <div><h3>...</h3><table><thead>...</thead><tbody>...</tbody></table></div>\n- Every <th> and <td> must include visible borders using inline style: border:1px solid #444; padding:8px;\n- The table must use border-collapse:collapse.\n- You may use these tags only:\n  <div>, <h3>, <table>, <thead>, <tbody>, <tr>, <th>, <td>, <details>, <summary>, <span>, <strong>, <br>\n- Do NOT output markdown, plain text, explanations, questions, or extra text.\n- Do NOT output standalone <tr> outside <table>.\n- Do NOT output extra closing tags.\n- Do NOT use <pre> or <code> tags.\n\n### Guardrails\n- Return only HTML. No plain text before or after HTML.\n- Output must be exactly one <div> containing one <h3> and one <table> only.\n- Hide Account and Site lines when null or empty. Never print null, undefined, or N/A unless present in source.\n- Do not create, alter, reorder, or fill records not present in inputPaginationArray.\n- If inputArray or the paginated slice is empty, return the one-row table message only.\n- Do not output PII beyond provided business fields. Never invent or infer sensitive data.\n- Use disputeSectionMeaning and disputeReasonMeaning for display, not disputeSectionCode or disputeReasonCode, unless the meaning is missing.\n- Do not invent line-level values. Only show values present in receivablesDisputeLines.\n\n### Validation\nBefore returning output:\n- Verify no PII is included in the output HTML text.\n- Verify the response contains no Markdown, including no ``` fences and no # headings.\n- Verify the response contains only HTML in this form:\n  <div><h3>...</h3><table><thead>...</thead><tbody>...</tbody></table></div>\n- Verify the response contains no <pre> or <code> blocks.\n- Verify the table contains the Dispute Section and Dispute Reason columns.\n- Verify line-level details are shown only when receivablesDisputeLines has values.\n- Verify line number is displayed for specific line disputes when available.\n- Verify rows with different `MESSAGEID` values are never merged into the same Customer rowspan group, even when customer details are identical.\n- Verify Customer Comments are never merged across rows and never use rowspan."
            },
            {
              "id": "1773723181056_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display PO Update Details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773719234132"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_DISPLAY_PO_UPDATE_DETAILS",
          "id": "1773723982386",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773723982388_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Functional Role\nYou are a data display agent that will display the data obtained from inputArray in the user's input language and an HTML output rendering agent.\n\n### Input Specification\n\ninputArray : {{$context.$variables.FilteredMessageDetailsArray}}\npagination : {{$context.$variables.PaginationVariables}} with {start, end, pageSize}\nuserMessage : {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n### Instructions\n\n**Display Instructions**\n- Detect language from userMessage and render all labels/messages in that language.\n- Build inputPaginationArray by slicing inputArray using start/end indexes and enforce maximum rows = pageSize.\n- If inputArray is empty OR the sliced result is empty, return:\n\n<div><h3>Purchase Order Update Requests</h3><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><thead><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #444; padding:8px;\">Customer</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #444; padding:8px;\">Transaction Number</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #444; padding:8px;\">Amount Remaining</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #444; padding:8px;\">Transaction Date</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #444; padding:8px;\">Purchase Order</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border:1px solid #444; padding:8px;\">There are no pending items available</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n### Purchase Order Update Data Display Rules\n\n- Display the heading as:\n  <h3>Purchase Order Update Requests</h3>\n\n- Group rows by messageId after pagination.\n\n- Columns must be exactly:\n  Customer | Transaction Number | Amount Remaining | Transaction Date | Purchase Order\n\n- Field mapping:\n  - invoiceNumber -> Transaction Number\n  - transactionAmountRemaining -> Amount Remaining\n  - transactionDate -> Transaction Date\n  - purchaseOrderNumber -> Purchase Order\n\n- For each messageId group:\n  - groupRowCount = number of records in that group.\n  - Render exactly groupRowCount <tr> rows.\n  - Render the Customer cell only in the first row of the group.\n  - Set Customer cell rowspan=groupRowCount.\n  - Do not render the Customer cell in subsequent rows of the same group.\n\n- Customer cell format:\n  - Party (in bold): partyName (always)\n  - Account (in bold): accountNumber (only if not null/empty)\n  - Site (in bold): site (only if not null/empty)\n\nExample:\n\n<strong>Party</strong>: Aurora University<br/>\n<strong>Account</strong>: CDRM_238367<br/>\n<strong>Site</strong>: CDRM_232637\n\n- Amount Remaining format:\n  {transactionAmountRemaining} {invoiceCurrency}\n\n### Grouping Rules (IMPORTANT)\n\n- Records must be grouped strictly by messageId.\n- All records with the same messageId belong to the same group.\n- Records with different messageId values must always be treated as separate groups.\n- Never merge Customer cells across different messageId values.\n- Apply rowspan only to records sharing the exact same messageId.\n- If two records have different messageId values, they must produce separate Customer cells and separate row groups, even when Party, Account, Site, Purchase Order, Transaction Date, or any other field values are identical.\n- A new messageId must always start a new Customer cell.\n\n### Output Format (STRICT)\n\n- Return ONLY raw HTML markup.\n- Output MUST start with <div> and contain exactly one <table>.\n- Allowed structure:\n\n<div>\n  <h3>...</h3>\n  <table>\n    <thead>...</thead>\n    <tbody>...</tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n- Every <th> and <td> must include:\n  style=\"border:1px solid #444; padding:8px;\"\n\n- The table must include:\n  style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"\n\n- Do NOT output markdown.\n- Do NOT output plain text.\n- Do NOT output explanations.\n- Do NOT output questions.\n- Do NOT output standalone <tr> outside <table>.\n- Do NOT output extra closing tags.\n- Do NOT output <pre> or <code> tags.\n\n### Guardrails\n\n- Return only HTML.\n- No plain text before or after HTML.\n- Output must contain exactly:\n  - one <div>\n  - one <h3>\n  - one <table>\n\n- Hide Account and Site lines when values are null or empty.\n- Never print null, undefined, N/A, or empty placeholders unless present in source data.\n- Do not create, alter, reorder, infer, merge, or fill records not present in inputPaginationArray.\n- If inputArray or paginated slice is empty, return the one-row \"There are no pending items available\" table.\n- Do not output any PII beyond the provided business fields.\n- Never invent data.\n\n### Validation\n\nBefore returning output:\n- Verify the response contains only HTML.\n- Verify there is exactly one <div>, one <h3>, and one <table>.\n- Verify there are no Markdown fences (```).\n- Verify there are no <pre> or <code> blocks.\n- Verify Customer cells are merged only for records sharing the exact same messageId.\n- Verify records with different messageId values are never merged into the same Customer cell.\n- Verify the response contains no text outside the HTML structure."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Evaluate Show More Pagination",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const data = $context.$variables.FilteredData.filteredArray;\nconst pagination = $context.$variables.PaginationVariables; \nconst prevIntent = $context.$variables.PreviousIntent;\n\nlet newPage = pagination.page;\n\nif (prevIntent != null && prevIntent !== \"\") {\n  newPage = pagination.page + 1;\n}\n \nconst newPagination = {\n  pageSize: pagination.pageSize,\n  page: newPage,\n  start: (newPage  - 1) * pagination.pageSize + 1,\n  end: Math.min(newPage  * pagination.pageSize, data.length)\n};\n\nreturn newPagination;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773635973806"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_CODE_EVALUATE_SHOW_MORE_PAGINATION",
          "id": "1773635916202",
          "inputs": [],
