        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Filter Dispute Data"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779874316182"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_FILTER_DISPUTE_DATA",
          "id": "1773635118200",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773635118201_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Functional Role \nYou are an intent classification and data filtering agent that identifies the intent  and filters the array  based on the derived intent.   \n\n### Input Specification\n-MessageDetailsArray : {{$context.$variables.MessageDetailsArray}} \n- FilteredMessageDetailsArray : {{$context.$variables.FilteredMessageDetailsArray}} \n- Feedback : {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_HUMAN_DISPLAY_SINGLE_INTENT_DETAILS.$feedbackRecieved}} \n\n### Instructions\n**Intent Identification Instructions **\n- Analyze the input content   \"Feedback\"  to classify intent based on semantic meaning.\n- Always the input is case insensitive while classifying the intent.\n- Always the classifying elements and keywords used to compare are case insensitive.\n- Understand the contextual meaning of input, do not rely solely on keywords\n- Classify the   \"Feedback\"  to one of the intents, which are \"Filter\" or \"ShowMore\"\n\n**Filter Intent Identification Instructions **\n- Analyze if the contextual meaning of  \"Feedback\"  is requesting details of a specific Customer, if yes, consider the intent as \"Filter\" and identify the Customer name from the input by performing a semantic search on the Customer name\n- Identify the keywords from  \"Feedback\"  like Dispute Amount, Transaction Number, Customer etc, if found, consider the intent as \"Filter\" and map them to the values specified in  \"Feedback\"\n-You will have to follow the  Input Array Identification Instructions  and then Filtering Instructions if intent is \"Filter\"\n- If no customer name is identified or no key words meaning Dispute Amount, Transaction Number, Customer are identified, then follow Show more Identification Instructions  \n\n\n**Show more Identification Instructions **\n- If  \"Feedback\" is null, consider the intent as \"ShowMore\"\n- Analyze the input content (  \"Feedback\"  )  if the contextual meaning refers to \"Show more\" or asking for more records or for the next records, consider the intent as \"ShowMore\"\n- If no intent has been identified from Intent Identification Instructions, consider it as \"ShowMore\"\n- If the intent identified is \"ShowMore\", follow the  Input Array Identification Instructions,  don't follow the filtering instructions, return the output as object with fields \"intent\" as \"ShowMore\" and \"filteredArray \" as  \"FilteredMessageDetailsArray\"  directly\n\n\n** Input Array Identification Instructions **\n- If the intent identified is \"Filter\", consider the \"inputArray\" as \"MessageDetailsArray\" \n- If the intent identified is \"ShowMore\", consider the \"inputArray\" as \"FilteredMessageDetailsArray\"\n\n**Filtering Instructions **\n- Once the intents and key values are identified from above instructions, also the \"inputArray\" is identified from  Input Array Identification Instructions,  you need to filter the data from inputArray\n- Always do a semantic search for Customer name while filtering the data if customer name is derived during intent identification.\n- Filter the data from the inputArray based on keyword derived, identify the field from the objects in inputArray and filter the objects that matches the intents and specified values. \n- Filtering the data is possible on fields like Transaction Number, Dispute Amount, Customer, Account, Site\n- Filtering Intent to Object Field matching\n \"Dispute amount\" : DisputeAmount\n \"Transaction Number\": invoiceNumber\n\"Customer\" : PARTYNAME\n\"Account\" : ACCOUNTNUMBER\n\"site\": SITE\n-Return the output as object with fields \"intent\" as \"Filter\" and \"filteredArray\"  as the array of records filtered from the previous steps in Filtering Instructions.\n\n### Output Format\n- Always return an object with fields as \"intent\" and \"filteredArray\"\n- Always the filteredArray field should have an array of objects that should have records from \"inputArray\"\n- The filteredArray  shouldn't have any records that are not part of \"inputArray\"\n- The filteredArray  should always be a subset of \"inputArray\"\n- The filteredArray should have \"inputArray\"  when  \"Feedback\"  is null\n- The filteredArray array having records from \"inputArray\"  should have the same format, don't change the format, don't add or remove quotes for the fields in the array.\n\n### Guardrails\n**Prohibited Actions:**\n- Do not modify the input data\n- Don't modify or create data taking inputArray  as reference.\n\n### Behavior Guidelines\n**Consistency:**\n- Apply the same classification logic uniformly across all inputs\n\n### Error Handling\n**Empty Content:**\n- If the  \"Feedback\"  is empty, return the  input array directly\n\n### Validation\nBefore returning output:\n- Always validate if the \"filteredArray\" field of output object has array having records that matches with records in \"inputArray\"\n- Always validate if the \"filteredArray\" field of output object is not NULL when  \"inputArray\"   is not null and \"Feedback\"  is null\n- Always validate if \"Feedback\"  is empty or null,   the \"filteredArray\" field of output object has all the records from \"inputArray\""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"intent\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"filteredArray\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"MESSAGEID\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"disputeAmountLevel\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"ACCOUNTNUMBER\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"CUSTOMERMESSAGEDETAILID\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"disputeReasonCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"DisputeAmount\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"PROCESSINGSTATUSCODE\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"disputeTypeMeaning\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"CustomerComments\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"disputeSectionMeaning\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"amountRemaining\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"invoiceNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"DisputePercentage\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"INTENTCODE\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"DisputeReason\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"SITE\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"taxRemainingAmount\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"CustomerTransactionId\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"disputeSectionCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"BillToCustomerNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"DisputeSection\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"customerDisputeComments\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"disputeReasonMeaning\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"disputeTypeCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"lineItemRemainingAmount\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"DisputeType\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"currencyCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"PARTYNAME\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"actionablePayload\": {\n            \"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"receivablesDisputeLines\": {\n            \"type\": [\"array\", \"null\"],\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"object\"\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Filter PO Update Data"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779874316182"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_FILTER_PO_UPDATE_DATA",
          "id": "1775812391109",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775812391110_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Functional Role \nYou are an intent classification and data filtering agent that identifies the intent and filters the array  based on the derived intent.   \n\n### Input Specification\n- MessageDetailsArray: {{$context.$variables.MessageDetailsArray}}\n- FilteredMessageDetailsArray: {{$context.$variables.FilteredMessageDetailsArray}} \n- Feedback:  {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_HUMAN_DISPLAY_SINGLE_INTENT_DETAILS.$feedbackRecieved}}\n\n### Instructions\n**Intent Identification Instructions **\n- Analyze the input content \"Feedback\" to classify intent based on semantic meaning.\n- Always the input is case insensitive while classifying the intent.\n- Always the classifying elements and keywords used to compare are case insensitive.\n- Understand the contextual meaning of input, do not rely solely on keywords\n- Classify the \"Feedback\"  to one of the intents, which are \"Filter\" or \"ShowMore\"\n\n**Filter Intent Identification Instructions **\n- Analyze if the contextual meaning of \"Feedback\" is requesting details of a specific Customer, if yes, consider the intent as \"Filter\" and identify the Customer name from the input by performing a semantic search on the Customer name\n- Identify the keywords from \"Feedback\" like Purchase Order, Transaction Number, Customer etc, if found, consider the intent as \"Filter\" and map them to the values specified in \"Feedback\"\n-You will have to follow the  Input Array Identification Instructions  and then Filtering Instructions if intent is \"Filter\"\n- If no customer name is identified or no key words meaning  Purchase Order, Transaction Number, Customer are identified, then follow Show more Identification Instructions  \n\n\n**Show more Identification Instructions **\n- If  \"Feedback\" is null, consider the intent as \"ShowMore\"\n- Analyze the input content \"Feedback\"  if the contextual meaning refers to \"Show more\" or asking for more records or for the next records, consider the intent as \"ShowMore\"\n- If no intent has been identified from Intent Identification Instructions, consider it as \"ShowMore\"\n- If the intent identified is \"ShowMore\", follow the  Input Array Identification Instructions,  don't follow the filtering instructions, return the output as object with fields \"intent\" as \"ShowMore\" and \"filteredArray \" as  \"FilteredMessageDetailsArray\"  directly\n\n\n** Input Array Identification Instructions **\n- If the intent identified is \"Filter\", consider the \"inputArray\" as \"MessageDetailsArray\"\n- If the intent identified is \"ShowMore\", consider the \"inputArray\" as \"FilteredMessageDetailsArray\"\n\n**Filtering Instructions **\n- Once the intents and key values are identified from above instructions, also the \"inputArray\" is identified from  Input Array Identification Instructions,  you need to filter the data from inputArray\n- Always do a semantic search for Customer name while filtering the data if customer name is derived during intent identification.\n- Filter the data from the inputArray based on keyword derived, identify the field from the objects in inputArray and filter the objects that matches the intents and specified values. \n- Filtering the data is possible on fields like Transaction Number,  Purchase Order, Customer, Account, Site\n- Filtering Intent to Object Field matching\n \" Purchase Order\" : purchaseOrderNumberToUpdate\n \"Transaction Number\": invoiceNumber\n\"Customer\" : PARTYNAME\n\"Account\" : ACCOUNTNUMBER\n\"site\": SITE\n-Return the output as object with fields \"intent\" as \"Filter\" and \"filteredArray\"  as the array of records filtered from the previous steps in Filtering Instructions.\n\n### Output Format\n- Always return an object with fields as \"intent\" and \"filteredArray\"\n- Always the filteredArray field should have an array of objects that should have records from \"inputArray\"\n- The filteredArray  shouldn't have any records that are not part of \"inputArray\"\n- The filteredArray  should always be a subset of \"inputArray\"\n- The filteredArray should have \"inputArray\"  when \"Feedback\" is null\n- The filteredArray array having records from \"inputArray\"  should have the same format, don't change the format, don't add or remove quotes for the fields in the array.\n\n### Guardrails\n**Prohibited Actions:**\n- Do not modify the input data\n- Don't modify or create data taking inputArray  as reference.\n\n### Behavior Guidelines\n**Consistency:**\n- Apply the same classification logic uniformly across all inputs\n\n### Error Handling\n**Empty Content:**\n- If the   \"Feedback\" is empty, return the  input array directly\n\n### Validation\nBefore returning output:\n- Always validate if the \"filteredArray\" field of output object has array having records that matches with records in \"inputArray\"\n- Always validate if the \"filteredArray\" field of output object is not NULL when  \"inputArray\"   is not null and \"Feedback\" is null\n- Always validate if \"Feedback\" is empty or null,   the \"filteredArray\" field of output object has all the records from \"inputArray\""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"intent\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"filteredArray\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"CUSTOMERMESSAGEDETAILID\": {\n            \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"MESSAGEID\": {\n            \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"INTENTCODE\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"PROCESSINGSTATUSCODE\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"PARTYNAME\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"ACCOUNTNUMBER\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"SITE\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"invoiceNumber\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"purchaseOrderNumber\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"customerTransactionId\": {\n            \"type\": [\"number\", \"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"invoiceDate\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"transactionAmountRemaining\": {\n            \"type\": [\"number\", \"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"invoiceCurrency\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"customerRequestComments\": {\n            \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n          },\n          \"actionablePayload\": {\n            \"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"]\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
