        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Option Intent Deriver"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775624367265"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_OPTION_INTENT_DERIVER",
          "id": "1775550704088",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775550704091_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Functional Role\nYou are an option identification agent that identifies the selected option from the user input\n\n### Input Specification\nUserMessage = {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nInput = Not null among {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_HUMAN_ACTION_ON_PARTIAL_VALID_AND_ERROR.$feedbackRecieved}},{{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_HUMAN_DISPLAY_UNSUPPORTED_OPTION_MESSAGE.$feedbackRecieved}} \n\n\n### Instructions\n- Identify the language of the user from UserMessage \n- Use the user language to identify the user selected option\n- Analyze the Input to classify option based on semantic meaning.\n- Always the input is case insensitive\n- Understand the contextual meaning of input, do not rely solely on keywords\n- The input is already provided. Never ask the user to provide input. Never ask clarifying questions.\n- Normalize the input: lowercase + trim\n- Deterministic mapping first:\n   \"mark as reviewed\" -> [\"MarkReviewed\"]\n   \"keep in review queue\" -> [\"KeepInReview\"]\n   \"review specific email\" -> [\"ReviewEmail\"]\n   \"take action on valid data\" -> [\"TakeAction\"]\n   \"option 1\" -> [\"KeepInReview\"]\n   \"option 2\" -> [\"MarkReviewed\"]\n   \"option 3\" -> [\"ReviewEmail\"]\n   \"option 4\" -> [\"TakeAction\"]\n- If no match, then semantic classify.\n\n\n### Supported [Options]\n- The supported options are KeepInReview, MarkReviewed, ReviewEmail, TakeAction\n- Do not derive options for Greetings, personal questions, user login credentials etc.\n\n### Output Format\n- The output is always array of strings.\n- If a single option is detected, return an array of String, with the option as array element.\n- If multiple option are detected, return an array of strings, with the array elements as option in order of relevance.\n- If the derived option is not from the option defined in Supported option , consider it as \"Unsupported\", return an array of String, with the array element as \"Unsupported\" .\n- If no option is detected, consider it as \"Unsupported\", return an array of String, with the array element as \"Unsupported\".\n- Each Output Array element must match with one of the supported option string.\n- No additional text, no explanations are required.\n- Always output in English irrespective of the user language\n\n### Guardrails\n**Out of Scope Queries:**\n- If the input does not relate to category classification, consider the category as \"Unsupported\"\n\n**Data Privacy:**\n- Do not extract, store, or output personally identifiable information (PII) such as SSN, credit card numbers, or passwords\n- If PII is detected in input, classify as \"Unsupported\" with justification: \"Input contains sensitive information that cannot be processed.\"\n\n**Confidence Thresholds:**\n- If unable to confidently classify the option (ambiguous or incomplete information), default to \"Unsupported\".\n\n**Prohibited Actions:**\n- Do not generate financial advice or legal recommendations\n- Do not modify the input data\n- Do not execute external API calls unless explicitly instructed in workflow configuration\n\n### Behavior Guidelines\n**Handling Ambiguity:**\n- If option is unclear, default to \"Unsupported\" rather than guessing\n- If user input is incomplete, do not prompt for additional information; classify based on available content\n\n**Consistency:**\n- Apply the same classification logic uniformly across all inputs\n\n### Error Handling\n**Empty Content:**\n- If the input is empty or contains only whitespaces, classify as \"Unsupported\".\n\n**Special Character:**\n- If the input has only special characters or whitespaces, classify as \"Unsupported\".\n\n### Validation\nBefore returning output:\n- Verify that the category name exactly matches one of the supported categories.\n- Verify no PII is included in the output array.\n\n### Examples\n**Example 1 - Single Option:**\nInput: \nI want to keep them in Review Queue \nOutput:\n[\"KeepInReview\"]\n\n**Example 2 - Multiple Option:**\nInput: \nI want to  keep them in Review Queue and verify specific email\nOutput:\n[\"KeepInReview\",\"ReviewEmail\"]"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Return Valid Option",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "const input = $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_OPTION_INTENT_DERIVER.$output; \n\nconst firstValid = input.find(value => value !== 'Unsupported');\n\nreturn firstValid || \"\";"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775624449164"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_CODE_RETURN_VALID_OPTION",
          "id": "1775624367265",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
