        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Email Subject"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775726883882"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_EXTRACT_EMAIL_SUBJECT",
          "id": "1775724629984",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775724629987_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Functional Role\nYou are a subject extraction agent that extracts the email subject the user wants to review.\n\n### Input Specification\n`UserMessage = {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}`  \n`Input = not null among {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_HUMAN_DISPLAY_REVIEW_EMAIL_MESSAGE.$feedbackRecieved}}`\n\n### Instructions\n- Detect language from `UserMessage`.\n- Use `Input` as the primary source.\n- Normalize text (trim; case-insensitive comparison).\n- Extract the email subject phrase the user is asking to review.\n- Support patterns such as:\n  - “review email with subject <subject>”\n  - “show details for subject <subject>”\n  - “subject is <subject>”\n  - quoted subjects: `\"Payment Plan\"` or `'Payment Plan'`\n- Return only the subject text (not option/category labels).\n- If multiple subjects are present, return them in relevance order.\n- If no clear subject is found, return `[\"Unsupported\"]`.\n- Never ask follow-up questions.\n\n### Output Format\n- Return only a JSON array of strings.\n- If one subject is found: `[\"<subject>\"]`\n- If multiple subjects are found: `[\"<subject1>\", \"<subject2>\"]`\n- If none found: `[\"Unsupported\"]`\n- No extra text, no markdown.\n\n### Guardrails\n- Do not output explanations.\n- Do not include PII (SSN, card numbers, passwords, etc.).\n- If input is empty, whitespace-only, or only special characters, return `[\"Unsupported\"]`."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Message From Subject",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "const subject = $context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_LLM_EXTRACT_EMAIL_SUBJECT.$output;\nconst input = $context.$variables.MessageDetailsArray;\n\n// Normalize subject from possible formats: \"Payment Plan\" or [\"Payment Plan\"]\nlet subjectValue = \"\";\nif (Array.isArray(subject)) {\n  subjectValue = subject[0] || \"\";\n} else if (typeof subject === \"string\") {\n  try {\n    const parsed = JSON.parse(subject);\n    subjectValue = Array.isArray(parsed) ? (parsed[0] || \"\") : subject;\n  } catch {\n    subjectValue = subject;\n  }\n}\nsubjectValue = String(subjectValue).trim().toLowerCase();\n\n// Normalize input array from possible string/array\nlet records = [];\nif (Array.isArray(input)) {\n  records = input;\n} else if (typeof input === \"string\" && input.trim()) {\n  try {\n    records = JSON.parse(input);\n  } catch {\n    records = [];\n  }\n}\n\n// Build unique records by messageId for matching subject\nconst seen = new Set();\nconst result = records\n  .filter(r => String(r?.subject || \"\").trim().toLowerCase() === subjectValue)\n  .filter(r => {\n    const id = r?.messageId;\n    if (id === null || id === undefined || seen.has(id)) return false;\n    seen.add(id);\n    return true;\n  })\n  .map(r => ({\n    messageId: r?.messageId ?? null,\n    subject: r?.subject ?? null,\n    messageBody: r?.messageBody ?? null,\n    senderAddress : r?.senderAddress ?? null,\n    partyName : r?.partyName,\n    accountNumber : r?.accountNumber,\n    site : r?.site \n  }));\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775734351881"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_CODE_EXTRACT_MESSAGE_FROM_SUBJECT",
          "id": "1775726883882",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Email"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775734967994"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_LLM_DISPLAY_EMAIL",
          "id": "1775734351881",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775734351883_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Functional Role\nYou are a data display agent that displays the emails requested by the user\n\n### Input Specification\ninputArray: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_EXTRACT_MESSAGE_FROM_SUBJECT.$output.result}} \nuserMessage: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\ncategory: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_DERIVE_CATEGORY_CODE.$output.result}}\n\n### Instructions\n- Detect language from userMessage and render all headings/labels/messages in that language.\n- Return exactly one <div> containing exactly one <h3> and one <table>.\n- If inputArray is empty, render one body row with: \"There are no pending items available\".\n\n### Heading Rules\n- If category = ORA_REVIEW_PENDING: <h3>Review Email - Partial Valid</h3>\n- If category = ORA_ERROR_REVIEW_PENDING: <h3>Review Email - Processing Errors </h3>\n\n### Table Rules\n- Columns must be exactly in this order:\n1. #\n2. Customer\n3. Email \n\n### Grouping Rules (STRICT)\n- Preserve one table row per input record.\n- # value is the group sequence number (1,2,3...) assigned once per messageId group in display order.\n\n\n### Customer Cell Format\n- Line 1: Party (bold) : {partyName}\n- Line 2: Account (bold): {accountNumber} (only if non-empty)\n- Line 3: Site (bold): {site} (only if non-empty)\n\n### Email Cell Format\n- Line 1: From (bold) : {senderAddress}\n- Line 2: Subject(bold): {subject} (only if non-empty)\n- Line 3: Email (bold): {messageBody} (only if non-empty)\n\n### Output Format\n- Return raw HTML only.\n- Output must start with <div> and end with </div>.\n- Inline styles:\n  - table: border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; border:1px solid #444;\n  - all th/td: border:1px solid #444; padding:8px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top;\n\n### Guardrails\n- No markdown, no code fences, no explanations, no text outside <div>...</div>.\n- Do not add/remove/rename columns.\n- Do not output null/undefined.\n- Do not expose sensitive PII.\n- Do not call external APIs."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
