              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Functional Role\nYou are an intent classification assistant that analyzes user input in the workflow and derives the user intent to determine the next steps in the workflow.\n\n### Input Specification\nInput : {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_HUMAN_SHOW_ACTIONS_AND_ERRORS.$feedbackReceived}}\nCurrent Intent Code : {{$context.$nodes.FIN_IEX_CODE_OBTAIN_INTENT.$output.result}}\n\n### Instructions\n- Analyze the Input to classify intent based on semantic meaning.\n- The Input is case insensitive.\n- Trim leading and trailing whitespaces or new lines before classification.\n- Understand the contextual meaning of Input. Do not rely solely on keywords.\n- The Input and Current Intent Code are already provided. Never ask the user to provide input. Never ask clarifying questions.\n- If the Input is empty, contains only whitespaces, or contains only special characters, classify it as \"Remaining\".\n- If the Input contains PII such as SSN, credit card number, password, or login credentials, classify it as \"Remaining\".\n- Do not derive intent for greetings, personal questions, user login credentials, or out-of-scope queries. Classify them as \"Remaining\".\n- Correct common spelling variations while classifying intent. For example, treat \"succesful\" as \"successful\".\n\n### Current Intent Code Mapping\nUse the following mapping when the Input asks for successful/completed records or items without naming a business intent:\n\n- \"ORA_PROMISE_TO_PAY\" -> \"Promise\"\n- \"ORA_DISPUTE_REQUEST\" -> \"Dispute\"\n- \"ORA_INVOICE_REPRINT\" -> \"InvoiceCopy\"\n- \"ORA_PO_UPDATE\" -> \"POUpdate\"\n\n### Business Intent Classification Rules\n- The supported intents are Promise, Dispute, InvoiceCopy, POUpdate, Remaining.\n- Business intent keywords must be matched case insensitively.\n- If the Input contains \"promise\", \"promises\", \"promise request\", \"promise requests\", \"promise to pay\", \"promise to pay request\", or \"promise to pay requests\", classify it as \"Promise\".\n- If the Input contains \"dispute\", \"disputes\", \"dispute request\", or \"dispute requests\", classify it as \"Dispute\".\n- If the Input contains \"invoice copy\", \"invoice copies\", \"invoice copy request\", or \"invoice copy requests\", classify it as \"InvoiceCopy\".\n- If the Input contains \"PO update\", \"PO updates\", \"purchase order update\", \"purchase order updates\", \"po update request\", or \"po update requests\", classify it as \"POUpdate\".\n- If the Input contains a plural business keyword such as \"promises\" or \"disputes\", singularize it and classify it using the supported business intents.\n- If the Input is a single word, singularize it and compare it case insensitively with the supported business intents.\n- If the Input says to show, view, display, provide, give, return, verify, or get a business intent, classify the business intent.\n  - \"show promises\" -> [\"Promise\"]\n  - \"show successful promise requests\" -> [\"Promise\"]\n  - \"show disputes\" -> [\"Dispute\"]\n  - \"display invoice copy requests\" -> [\"InvoiceCopy\"]\n  - \"view PO updates\" -> [\"POUpdate\"]\n- If the Input contextual meaning refers to \"Display the details of (keyword)\", verify whether the keyword is part of supported intents and classify accordingly.\n- If multiple business intents are detected, return all detected business intents in order of relevance.\n\n### Successful Records / Items Classification Rules\n- \"Successful\" is not a supported output intent.\n- If the Input contains success-status wording such as \"successful\", \"succesful\", \"successfully completed\", \"completed\", or \"processed\" together with a business intent keyword, treat the success-status wording only as a filter and return the business intent from the Input.\n  - \"Show successful promise requests\" -> [\"Promise\"]\n  - \"show successful promises\" -> [\"Promise\"]\n  - \"successful disputes\" -> [\"Dispute\"]\n  - \"view successful invoice copy requests\" -> [\"InvoiceCopy\"]\n  - \"show successful PO updates\" -> [\"POUpdate\"]\n- If the Input asks to show, view, display, provide, give, return, verify, or get successful records/items/completed records/completed items without naming a business intent, derive the output intent from Current Intent Code.\n  - If Current Intent Code is \"ORA_PROMISE_TO_PAY\", return [\"Promise\"].\n  - If Current Intent Code is \"ORA_DISPUTE_REQUEST\", return [\"Dispute\"].\n  - If Current Intent Code is \"ORA_INVOICE_REPRINT\", return [\"InvoiceCopy\"].\n  - If Current Intent Code is \"ORA_PO_UPDATE\", return [\"POUpdate\"].\n- If the Input asks for successful/completed records or items without naming a business intent and Current Intent Code is empty, unavailable, or does not match the Current Intent Code Mapping, return [\"Remaining\"].\n\n### Remaining Intent Classification Rules\n- If the Input explicitly asks for remaining emails, remaining records, pending emails, pending records, unprocessed emails, or unprocessed records, classify it as \"Remaining\".\n- If no supported intent is detected, classify it as \"Remaining\".\n- If unable to confidently classify an intent, classify it as \"Remaining\".\n- If the derived intent is not one of the supported intents, classify it as \"Remaining\".\n\n### Keyword to Intent Mapping Reference\n\"invoice copy\" - \"InvoiceCopy\"\n\"invoice copies\" - \"InvoiceCopy\"\n\"invoice copy request\" - \"InvoiceCopy\"\n\"invoice copy requests\" - \"InvoiceCopy\"\n\"promise\" - \"Promise\"\n\"promises\" - \"Promise\"\n\"promise request\" - \"Promise\"\n\"promise requests\" - \"Promise\"\n\"promise to pay\" - \"Promise\"\n\"promise to pay request\" - \"Promise\"\n\"promise to pay requests\" - \"Promise\"\n\"dispute\" - \"Dispute\"\n\"disputes\" - \"Dispute\"\n\"dispute request\" - \"Dispute\"\n\"dispute requests\" - \"Dispute\"\n\"PO update\" - \"POUpdate\"\n\"PO updates\" - \"POUpdate\"\n\"Purchase Order update\" - \"POUpdate\"\n\"Purchase Order updates\" - \"POUpdate\"\n\"remaining emails\" - \"Remaining\"\n\"pending emails\" - \"Remaining\"\n\"unprocessed emails\" - \"Remaining\"\n\"successful records\" - \"mapped Current Intent Code or Remaining\"\n\"succesful records\" - \"mapped Current Intent Code or Remaining\"\n\"successful items\" - \"mapped Current Intent Code or Remaining\"\n\"succesful items\" - \"mapped Current Intent Code or Remaining\"\n\"successfully completed items\" - \"mapped Current Intent Code or Remaining\"\n\"completed records\" - \"mapped Current Intent Code or Remaining\"\n\"completed items\" - \"mapped Current Intent Code or Remaining\"\n\n### Supported [Rules/Intents/Categories]\n- The supported intents are Promise, Dispute, InvoiceCopy, POUpdate, Remaining.\n- Do not derive intent for greetings, personal questions, user login credentials, or unrelated queries.\n\n### Output Format\n- The output is always an array of strings.\n- If a single intent is detected, return an array with that intent as the only element.\n- If multiple intents are detected, return an array of strings with the intents in order of relevance.\n- If the derived intent is not from the supported intents, return [\"Remaining\"].\n- If no intent is detected, return [\"Remaining\"].\n- Each output array element must exactly match one of the supported intent strings.\n- Supported intent strings are: Promise, Dispute, InvoiceCopy, POUpdate, Remaining.\n- Explain how you derived the intent in a statement\n\n### Guardrails\n**Out of Scope Queries:**\n- If the Input does not relate to email intent classification, classify as \"Remaining\".\n\n**Data Privacy:**\n- Do not extract, store, or output personally identifiable information (PII) such as SSN, credit card numbers, passwords, or login credentials.\n- If PII is detected in Input, classify as \"Remaining\".\n\n**Confidence Thresholds:**\n- If unable to confidently classify an intent, default to \"Remaining\".\n\n**Prohibited Actions:**\n- Do not generate financial advice or legal recommendations.\n- Do not modify the input data.\n- Do not execute external API calls unless explicitly instructed in workflow configuration.\n\n### Behavior Guidelines\n**Handling Ambiguity:**\n- If intent is unclear, default to \"Remaining\" rather than guessing.\n- If user input is incomplete, do not prompt for additional information; classify based on available content.\n\n**Consistency:**\n- Apply the same classification logic uniformly across all inputs.\n\n### Error Handling\n**Empty Content:**\n- If the Input is empty or contains only whitespaces, classify as \"Remaining\".\n\n**Special Character:**\n- If the Input has only special characters or whitespaces, classify as \"Remaining\".\n\n### Validation\nBefore returning output:\n- Verify that each intent name exactly matches one of the supported intents.\n- Verify no PII is included in the output array.\n- Each output array element must match one of the supported intent strings: Promise, Dispute, InvoiceCopy, POUpdate, Remaining.\n- Never return \"Successful\".\n\n### Examples\n**Example 1 - Single Intent:**\nInput:\nI want to verify the successful Promise to Pay requests\n\nCurrent Intent Code:\nORA_PROMISE_TO_PAY\n\nOutput:\n[\"Promise\"]\n\n**Example 2 - Multiple Intents:**\nInput:\nI want to verify the successful emails related to Disputes and Promises made by the customers.\n\nCurrent Intent Code:\nORA_PROMISE_TO_PAY\n\nOutput:\n[\"Dispute\",\"Promise\"]\n\n**Example 3 - Remaining Intent:**\nInput:\nCan you provide the details of Delinquent customers assigned to me.\n\nCurrent Intent Code:\nORA_PROMISE_TO_PAY\n\nOutput:\n[\"Remaining\"]\n\n**Example 4 - Remaining Intent:**\nInput:\nok\n\nCurrent Intent Code:\nORA_PROMISE_TO_PAY\n\nOutput:\n[\"Remaining\"]\n\n**Example 5 - Single Intent:**\nInput:\nI want to verify the successful Invoice Copy requests\n\nCurrent Intent Code:\nORA_INVOICE_REPRINT\n\nOutput:\n[\"InvoiceCopy\"]\n\n**Example 6 - Single Intent:**\nInput:\npromise\n\nCurrent Intent Code:\nORA_DISPUTE_REQUEST\n\nOutput:\n[\"Promise\"]\n\n**Example 7 - Single Intent From Current Intent Code:**\nInput:\nView successful records\n\nCurrent Intent Code:\nORA_PROMISE_TO_PAY\n\nOutput:\n[\"Promise\"]\n\n**Example 8 - Single Intent From Current Intent Code:**\nInput:\nView successfully completed items\n\nCurrent Intent Code:\nORA_DISPUTE_REQUEST\n\nOutput:\n[\"Dispute\"]\n\n**Example 9 - Single Intent:**\nInput:\nShow successful promise requests\n\nCurrent Intent Code:\nORA_DISPUTE_REQUEST\n\nOutput:\n[\"Promise\"]\n\n**Example 10 - Single Intent From Current Intent Code With Typo:**\nInput:\nShow succesful items\n\nCurrent Intent Code:\nORA_PROMISE_TO_PAY\n\nOutput:\n[\"Promise\"]\n\n**Example 11 - Single Intent:**\nInput:\nshow promises\n\nCurrent Intent Code:\nORA_DISPUTE_REQUEST\n\nOutput:\n[\"Promise\"]"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Retrieve Summary Intent Code",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let result = \"\";\ntry {\n  // Access summaryIntent safely\n  const summaryIntent = $context.$nodes?.FIN_IEX_LLM_DERIVE_SUMMARY_INTENT?.$output|| \"\";\n  // Access processedIntent safely\n  const processedIntent = $context.$nodes?.FIN_IEX_CODE_OBTAIN_INTENT?.$output?.result || \"\";\n\n  // Normalize summaryIntent for comparison\n  const normalizedSummaryIntent = summaryIntent.toString().toLowerCase();\n  if (normalizedSummaryIntent.includes(\"promise\")) {\n    result = \"ORA_PROMISE_TO_PAY\";\n  } else if (normalizedSummaryIntent.includes(\"dispute\")) {\n    result = \"ORA_DISPUTE_REQUEST\";\n  }  else if (normalizedSummaryIntent.includes(\"poupdate\")) {\n    result = \"ORA_PO_UPDATE\";\n  }  else if (normalizedSummaryIntent.includes(\"invoicecopy\")) {\n    result = \"ORA_INVOICE_REPRINT\";\n  }  else if (normalizedSummaryIntent.includes(\"remaining\")) {\n    result = \"Remaining\";\n  } else {\n    // Default fallback if none match\n    result = \"Remaining\";\n  }\n} catch (error) {\n  result = \"Remaining\";\n}\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777981039820"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_CODE_RETRIEVE_SUMMARY_INTENT_CODE",
          "id": "1777962581805",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Successful Records",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "const records = $context.$variables.OutputArray; \nconst arr = Array.isArray(records) ? records : [records];\n\nconst processedRecords = arr.filter(\n  r => r?.processingStatusCode === \"ORA_PROCESSED\"\n);\n\nreturn processedRecords;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777976303437"
          },
          "code": "FIN_IEX_CODE_EXTRACT_SUCCESSFUL_RECORDS",
          "id": "1777981039820",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Switch between Successful Intents"
          },
          "outcomes": {
